.v2.schema.json, https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/schemas/lsp-trace.unified-structural-context-result.v3.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead. Before live semantic analysis, call lsp_session_v1_list and use an exact-workspace READY session. If none exists and the target is an exact registered Git worktree, call lsp_session_v1_derive_workspace with exactly one READY parent and the target's canonical absolute local file: URI; continue only from its READY result. Do not start an independently configured replacement language server. Choose the transport explicitly: Direct MCP operation calls pass that operation's arguments directly; for MCP gateway `lsp_trace_v1_execute`, operation is nested beneath `request`, for example {\"request\":{\"operation\":\"lsp_trace_v2_structural_context\",\"arguments\":{...}}}; CLI `lsp-trace execute` accepts production execution requests and is not an MCP dispatcher. MCP wire and server operation names are canonical unqualified names; host adapters may display namespace-qualified names. `request.operation` always uses the canonical unqualified operation name. If capabilities or the installed revision advertise an operation but the client does not list it or its tool schema rejects it before dispatch, reconnect or refresh MCP metadata before diagnosing the language server. The MCP gateway is a dispatch interface and does not bypass stale client-side schema validation. Distinguish client or adapter schema validation from server dispatch, structural preflight, and traversal typed failures.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_trace_v2_structural_context(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"$id":"https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-structural-context.v6.schema.json","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"oneOf":[{"not":{"anyOf":[{"required":["uri"]},{"required":["line"]},{"required":["character"]},{"required":["regex_locator"]}]},"required":["symbol"]},{"not":{"anyOf":[{"required":["symbol"]},{"required":["regex_locator"]}]},"required":["uri","line","character"]},{"not":{"anyOf":[{"required":["symbol"]},{"required":["uri"]},{"required":["line"]},{"required":["character"]}]},"required":["regex_locator"]},{"not":{"anyOf":[{"required":["line"]},{"required":["character"]},{"required":["regex_locator"]}]},"properties":{"down_depth":{"const":0},"projection":{"properties":{"include_relation_occurrences":{"const":false},"mode":{"const":"TARGET"}},"required":["mode","include_relation_occurrences"],"type":"object"},"up_depth":{"const":0}},"required":["symbol","uri","projection","up_depth","down_depth"]}],"properties":{"analysis":{"default":{"kind":"NEIGHBORHOOD"},"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"const":"NEIGHBORHOOD"}},"required":["kind"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"depth":{"maximum":64,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"direction":{"enum":["INCOMING","OUTGOING"]},"kind":{"const":"IMPACT"}},"required":["kind","direction","depth"],"type":"object"}]},"character":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"down_depth":{"default":1,"maximum":64,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"generation":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"language_id":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"line":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_bytes":{"default":4194304,"maximum":16777216,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_messages":{"default":64,"maximum":4096,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_nodes":{"default":100,"maximum":10000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"projection":{"$id":"https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/source-projection-request.v3.schema.json","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"description":"Optional bounded source projection. Omit this object for relationship-only structural context. For source-bearing implementation or ownership analysis, use PROJECTED with INCLUDE and FULL_DEFINITION.","properties":{"body":{"description":"INCLUDE returns source bodies for selected full display ranges; OMIT returns metadata, ranges, custody, privacy, and accounting without source bodies.","enum":["OMIT","INCLUDE"]},"display_range_policy":{"const":"FULL_DEFINITION","description":"Resolve complete definition display ranges from server-reported textDocument/documentSymbol while preserving exact evidence, item, selection, and call-site ranges independently."},"include_ancillary":{"description":"Include eligible ancillary source only when explicitly requested; normally false for implementation analysis.","type":"boolean"},"include_relation_occurrences":{"description":"Include exact server-reported call-site occurrences and their containing caller definitions when selected by the projection mode.","type":"boolean"},"limits":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Independent hard projection and document-acquisition bounds. A practical bounded starting point is objects/ranges 80, source bytes 2097152, work 10000, response bytes 8388608, additional documents 20, document requests 21, document bytes 1048576, total document bytes 8388608, document messages 32, acquisition work 21, and display-resolution work 21.","properties":{"max_additional_documents":{"description":"Maximum selected non-target documents.","maximum":10000,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_display_resolution_work":{"description":"Maximum server-reported document-symbol display-resolution work units.","maximum":536870912,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_document_acquisition_work":{"description":"Maximum managed document-acquisition work units.","maximum":536870912,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_document_bytes":{"description":"Maximum bytes admitted for each prepared document.","maximum":16777216,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_document_messages":{"description":"Maximum protocol messages consumed by each document preparation.","maximum":4096,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_document_requests":{"description":"Maximum managed document preparation requests including the target.","maximum":10000,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_objects":{"description":"Maximum selected projection units.","maximum":10000,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_ranges":{"description":"Maximum selected source ranges.","maximum":10000,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_response_bytes":{"description":"Maximum complete encoded response bytes.","maximum":16777216,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_source_bytes":{"description":"Maximum unique returned source bytes.","maximum":16777216,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_total_document_bytes":{"description":"Maximum total bytes admitted across prepared documents.","maximum":67108864,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_work":{"description":"Maximum projection work units.","maximum":536870912,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["max_objects","max_ranges","max_source_bytes","max_work","max_response_bytes","max_additional_documents","max_document_requests","max_document_bytes","max_total_document_bytes","max_document_messages","max_document_acquisition_work","max_display_resolution_work"],"type":"object"},"mode":{"description":"TARGET returns only the target definition; PROJECTED returns selected endpoint definitions and exact server-reported relation occurrences; COMPLETE_CAPTURE additionally permits explicitly selected ancillary source.","enum":["TARGET","PROJECTED","COMPLETE_CAPTURE"]},"paging":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"maxLength":16384,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"max_page_bytes":{"maximum":1048576,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_pages":{"maximum":10000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_response_bytes":{"maximum":67108864,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["max_page_bytes","max_pages","max_response_bytes"],"type":"object"},"privacy_policy_id":{"description":"Caller-selected projection privacy policy identifier; use only a policy recognized by the executing host.","maxLength":256,"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["mode","body","include_relation_occurrences","include_ancillary","display_range_policy","limits","privacy_policy_id"],"type":"object"},"regex_locator":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"capture_group":{"maximum":32,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"expected_document_digest":{"pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","type":"string"},"limits":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"max_document_bytes":{"default":61440,"maximum":16777216,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_matches":{"default":100,"maximum":1000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_pattern_bytes":{"default":4096,"maximum":4096,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_work":{"default":65536,"maximum":536870912,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"type":"object"},"match_index":{"maximum":999,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"pattern":{"maxLength":4096,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"uri":{"format":"uri","type":"string"}},"required":["uri","pattern","match_index","limits"],"type":"object"},"request_timeout_ms":{"default":15000,"maximum":60000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"session_id":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"symbol":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"timeout_ms":{"default":30000,"maximum":60000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"up_depth":{"default":1,"maximum":64,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"uri":{"format":"uri","type":"string"}},"required":["session_id","generation"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"mcp__granola__query_granola_meetings","description":"Query Granola about the user's meetings using natural language. Returns a tailored response with inline citation links in markdown (e.g. [[1]](url)) that reference source meeting notes.\n\nIMPORTANT: The response includes numbered citation links to specific Granola meeting notes. These citations MUST be preserved in your response to the user — they provide transparency and allow the user to verify information by clicking through to the original notes.\n\nFor optional deeper reads, extract the meeting ID from the citation URL: https://notes.granola.ai/d/<meeting_id>. Pass that ID to get_meetings (meeting_ids).\n\nThis tool is slow: an AI agent behind it searches and reads the user's notes before answering. Prefer a faster tool when it can answer the question:\n- list_meetings: find meetings by date range\n- get_meetings: read notes for meetings whose IDs you already have\n\nWhen to use:\n- User asks about what was discussed, decided, or action-items from meetings\n- User asks about follow-ups, todos, or commitments from recent meetings\n- User references 'Granola notes' or 'meeting notes'\n\nWhen NOT to use:\n- User is asking about calendar scheduling or upcoming events\n- User explicitly asks for a specific meeting by ID (use get_meetings instead)\n\nPrioritize using query_granola_meetings over list_meetings/get_meetings for open-ended or natural language queries about meeting content.\n\nIf this tool does not find a requested detail, meeting summaries may have omitted it. Use list_meetings/get_meetings to identify the most relevant meetings, then get_meeting_transcript only where that meeting's workspace permits transcript access. If access is denied, report that limitation; do not retry through another tool or conclude the information was never discussed.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__query_granola_meetings(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The query to run on Granola meeting notes"},"document_ids":{"description":"Optional meeting UUIDs or public note IDs to limit context to (max 10).","maxItems":10,"type":"array","items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}],"description":"Meeting UUID or public note ID (not_…)"}},"note_ids":{"description":"Alias for document_ids (max 10). If both are provided, they must refer to the same set of notes; order, duplicates, and UUID/public ID format may differ.","maxItems":10,"type":"array","items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}],"description":"Meeting UUID or public note ID (not_…)"}}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"mcp__granola__list_meetings","description":"List the user's Granola meeting notes within a time range (the last 7 days by default). Returns meeting titles, metadata, and note URLs.\n\nIMPORTANT: For short-term questions about recent meeting details, prefer using query_granola_meetings instead.\n\nWhen to use:\n- User asks to list their meetings\n- User asks about action items, decisions, or summaries from meetings over a longer or specific date range\n- User asks about content from their meeting transcripts\n- User references 'Granola notes' or 'meeting notes' or 'transcripts'\n\nWhen NOT to use:\n- User is asking about upcoming calendar events or scheduling\n- User wants to create/modify calendar invites\n\nFiltering:\n- Omit workspace_only and involvement to return every meeting the user is allowed to access\n- For 'my meetings' or meetings the user was involved in, set both involvement conditions to true; true conditions combine using OR\n- Set captured_by_me to true for meetings whose Granola notes the user captured, or false to exclude them\n- Set listed_as_participant to true for meetings where the user is a known participant, or false to exclude them\n- False involvement conditions are exclusions and combine with the positive conditions using AND; omit a condition to ignore it\n- For Team Space or public workspace meetings, set workspace_only to true\n- workspace_only and involvement combine using AND\n\nUse get_meetings to retrieve detailed meeting content after identifying relevant meetings.\nUse list_meeting_folders to discover folder IDs, then pass a folder_id to list meetings within a specific folder.\nThe requested_range element reports the range that was queried, in the user's timezone. The from and to attributes on meetings_data are the oldest and newest meetings returned.\nMeetings with shared-screen screenshots you can view include a screenshot_count attribute; a meeting without it has none you can view. Use get_meetings to read what each screenshot shows.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__list_meetings(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"time_range":{"description":"Time range to query meetings from. Custom bounds imply 'custom' when time_range is omitted; otherwise defaults to the last 7 days, starting at midnight in the user's timezone.","type":"string","enum":["last_7_days","this_week","last_week","last_30_days","custom"]},"custom_start":{"description":"ISO date for custom range start (required if time_range is 'custom'). Prefer YYYY-MM-DD for whole-day requests; dates and times without an offset use the user's stored timezone (UTC if unavailable). An explicit Z means UTC; explicit offsets are respected. Do not append Z to a local time.","type":"string"},"custom_end":{"description":"ISO date for custom range end (required if time_range is 'custom'). Prefer YYYY-MM-DD to include the whole final day in the user's stored timezone (UTC if unavailable). Times without an offset use that timezone; an explicit Z means UTC and explicit offsets are respected. Do not append Z to a local time.","type":"string"},"folder_id":{"description":"Optional folder ID to list meetings from a specific folder. Requires a paid Granola plan. Use list_meeting_folders to discover folder IDs.","type":"string"},"workspace_only":{"description":"Set to true only when the user explicitly asks for Team Space, public workspace, or workspace-visible meetings. Omit to search every meeting the user is allowed to access.","type":"boolean","const":true},"involvement":{"description":"Optional involvement filter. Conditions set to true form an OR inclusion group. Conditions set to false are exclusions applied using AND. Omitted conditions are ignored.","type":"object","properties":{"captured_by_me":{"description":"True includes meetings whose Granola note was captured by the connected user; false excludes them; omit to ignore who captured the note. This identifies the note owner, not necessarily the meeting organizer.","type":"boolean"},"listed_as_participant":{"description":"True includes meetings where the connected user's email appears in Granola's known participant metadata; false excludes them; omit to ignore participant metadata. Participant metadata can be incomplete and does not prove attendance.","type":"boolean"}},"additionalProperties":false}},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"mcp__granola__list_meeting_folders","description":"List the user's Granola meeting folders. Returns folder ID, title, description, note count including nested folders, visibility (private or workspace) and who can see the folder's notes.\n\nWhen to use:\n- User asks about their folders or wants to browse meetings by folder\n- User wants to narrow down meeting searches to a specific folder\n\nUse the returned folder IDs with list_meetings (folder_id parameter) to list meetings within a specific folder.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__list_meeting_folders(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{}}},{"name":"mcp__granola__get_meetings","description":"Get detailed meeting information for one or more Granola meetings by ID. Returns private notes, AI-generated summary, attendees, metadata, and note URLs.\nDoes not return transcripts. Notes and summaries can omit details that were discussed.\nIf a detail is missing, use get_meeting_transcript on the most relevant meetings only where that meeting's workspace permits transcript access. If access is denied, report that limitation; do not retry through another tool or conclude it was never discussed.\nUse this when you already have specific meeting IDs (e.g. from list_meetings results). For open-ended questions about meeting content, use query_granola_meetings instead.\nMeetings where the user captured the shared screen include an <attachments> section listing each screenshot as an <attachment type=\"screenshot\"> with an ID and description. Descriptions are lossy. For questions about designs, UI, slides, charts, code or anything else visual, view the relevant screenshots with get_meeting_attachment rather than answering from descriptions.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__get_meetings(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"meeting_ids":{"description":"Meeting UUIDs or public note IDs (max 10).","minItems":1,"maxItems":10,"type":"array","items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}],"description":"Meeting UUID or public note ID (not_…)"}},"note_ids":{"description":"Alias for meeting_ids. If both are provided, they must refer to the same set of notes; order, duplicates, and UUID/public ID format may differ.","minItems":1,"maxItems":10,"type":"array","items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}],"description":"Meeting UUID or public note ID (not_…)"}}},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"mcp__granola__get_meeting_transcript","description":"Get the full transcript for a specific Granola meeting by ID. Returns only the verbatim transcript content, not summaries or notes.\nTranscript blocks separate audio source (Microphone/System audio) from speaker identity. Participant attribution and user-confirmed names are preserved. Desktop diarization is omitted; mobile/imported transcripts can retain Speaker A/B/... labels for unnamed voices. Recording context identifies the document owner as the recorder for native recordings, not as the speaker. Missing recorder data stays unknown; the current viewer is not substituted. Channels and room labels may include multiple people. Older preformatted transcripts keep their original labels.\nRequires access to the meeting and transcript access permitted by that meeting's workspace. Use this for exact quotes or when query_granola_meetings/get_meetings does not surface a requested detail, such as a person, example, or explanation. Start with the most relevant meetings; a detail missing from summaries may still be in the transcript. If access is denied, report that limitation and do not retry through another tool. For general summaries or action items, start with query_granola_meetings or get_meetings.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__get_meeting_transcript(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"meeting_id":{"description":"Meeting UUID or public note ID (not_…).","anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}]},"note_id":{"description":"Alias for meeting_id. If both are provided, they must refer to the same note (UUID and public note ID may differ).","anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}]}},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"mcp__granola__get_account_info","description":"Get the email, active workspace, joined workspaces (names and IDs), and effective note-access scopes for the Granola account currently connected to this MCP session.\n\nWorkspace membership does not imply MCP access to its meetings.\n\nmcp_plan is the effective plan used for MCP access and limits.\n\nWhen to use:\n- User asks 'who am I signed in as?', 'which Granola account is this?', or 'what's my email?'\n- User suspects they connected the wrong Granola account\n- User wants to sign out or switch accounts: use sign_out to revoke this client's authorization. No browser action is needed to complete MCP sign-out. To use another account, reconnect Granola in this client. Only if the browser automatically selects the previous account, open sign_out_url in that browser before reconnecting again.\n- User asks which workspaces they belong to or mentions another workspace\n- Meeting results may be missing because the wrong workspace is active\n- Meeting results may be incomplete or empty because of the user's Granola plan or workspace MCP access controls\n- Before performing actions, to confirm identity if the user references a specific account\n\nmcp_note_access.scopes contains the note categories this connection can search:\n- personal: notes the connected user owns, notes shared directly with them, and notes accessible through private folders\n- public: notes accessible through workspace-visible Team Space folders\n- Both scopes means both categories can be searched. These scopes describe access, not who captured or participated in a meeting.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__get_account_info(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{}}},{"name":"mcp__granola__sign_out","description":"Revoke the connected Granola account's consent and refresh tokens for this MCP client. Only use when the user asks to sign out, disconnect, or switch Granola accounts. This affects all connections for this account using the same client authorization. New MCP requests using this authorization will be rejected immediately after sign-out. No browser action is needed to complete MCP sign-out. If the user wants to switch accounts, tell them to reconnect Granola in this client. Only if the browser automatically selects their previous account, open the returned sign_out_url in that browser before reconnecting again.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__sign_out(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{}}},{"name":"mcp__granola__get_meeting_attachment","description":"Get up to 5 meeting attachments, such as screenshots of shared screens, as images in request order. Provide attachment_ids for a batch or attachment_id for one image. Each image is followed by its metadata; failed attachments return an error with their ID without discarding successful images. Attachment IDs come from the <attachments> section of get_meetings results. Use this when the description alone does not answer the user's question, for example to read a slide, chart, or code on screen.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__granola__get_meeting_attachment(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"type":"object","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"meeting_id":{"description":"Meeting UUID or public note ID (not_…).","anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}]},"note_id":{"description":"Alias for meeting_id. If both are provided, they must refer to the same note (UUID and public note ID may differ).","anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})$"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^not_[a-zA-Z0-9]{14}$"}]},"attachment_id":{"description":"Single attachment ID. Provide exactly one of attachment_id or attachment_ids.","type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$"},"attachment_ids":{"description":"Attachment IDs from the <attachment id=\"...\"> tags in get_meetings results. Provide exactly one of attachment_id or attachment_ids.","minItems":1,"maxItems":5,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$"}}},"additionalProperties":false}}]},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:19:38.890Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"1f290c50-b945-4fe","type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00fa2b2059da4eff88a84ff865a26bee|fc_03201568652b0503016ace4c09ec70819b98732e6c468229e0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn read /Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace/.pi/skills/lsp-trace-feature-inventory/SKILL.md","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1189,"output":48,"cacheRead":37248,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":38485,"cost":{"input":0.004756,"output":0.0009600000000000001,"cacheRead":0.014899200000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0206152}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791904776603,"responseId":"resp_03201568652b0503016ace4c08ef10819baca4ffc4f40b37ef","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"minimal"},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:19:38.890Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"1f290c50-b945-4fe","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00fa2b2059da4eff88a84ff865a26bee|fc_03201568652b0503016ace4c09ec70819b98732e6c468229e0","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t---\n2\tname: lsp-trace-feature-inventory\n3\tdescription: Prepare and review correction-safe feature inventories from bounded lsp-trace structural evidence. Use for mechanical inventory preparation, reversible grouping hypotheses, semantic adjudication, stakeholder correction, and accepted-inventory boundaries; never use structural evidence alone to accept feature identity.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# lsp-trace feature inventory\n7\t\n8\tUse this workflow when bounded technical evidence must inform a feature inventory. The inventory is external to native lsp-trace graph, inspection, filter, community, instability, and capture-set artifacts.\n9\t\n10\tLoad references progressively:\n11\t\n12\t- For evidence packet preparation, census inputs, accounting, provisional records, and reversible grouping, read [Preparation and grouping](references/preparation-and-grouping.md).\n13\t- For independent semantic review, stakeholder correction, acceptance, presentation, iteration, and stopping rules, read [Adjudication and acceptance](references/adjudication-and-acceptance.md).\n14\t- For structural command details or authority ceilings, also load the `lsp-trace` skill and its relevant reference.\n15\t\n16\t## Non-negotiable boundary\n17\t\n18\tMechanical preparation cannot accept feature identity. Technical adjacency, CALLS overlap, communities, centrality, instability, repeated labels, capture-set co-membership, or matching names are structural evidence only. They may nominate or challenge a hypothesis; they cannot decide canonical identity, purpose, value, production use, merge/split outcome, coverage, confidence, or acceptance.\n19\t\n20\tCALLS remains server-reported only. Capture sets preserve constituents without inferring cross-capture CALLS or acquiring native single-capture custody. Preserve bounded zero, `UNKNOWN`, failed/successful-empty states, and untouched ambiguity explicitly.\n21\t\n22\t## Workflow\n23\t\n24\t1. Retain a transport-neutral technical evidence packet and reconcile all seeds and counts.\n25\t2. Prepare external `PROVISIONAL` candidate records with exact typed evidence references, alternatives, rejection conditions, authority ceilings, and correction lineage.\n26\t3. Treat grouping as a reversible hypothesis. Communities and instability may organize review but do not change candidate identity or status.\n27\t4. Run independent semantic adjudication. Challenge unsupported merges/splits, borrowed union evidence, transitive-as-direct claims, and absence inferred from bounded zero or `UNKNOWN`.\n28\t5. Request stakeholder correction for product/domain meaning. Record corrections as revisions with predecessors and finite inventory-state deltas; never rewrite native evidence.\n29\t6. Accept an inventory only under an explicit external authority and acceptance contract. Otherwise stop as provisional, unresolved, externally adjudicated, accepted-boundary, or bounded-review-dry as applicable.\n30\t\n31\tThe documented CLI `census` command may be used for accountable source-symbol enumeration and batched acquisition; use only syntax printed by current executable help. Its structural output cannot accept feature identity or upgrade authority, completeness, custody, cross-capture CALLS, or Leiden admission. `context` is AVAILABLE for bounded transient live structural analysis; use only current help or capability syntax and do not treat its output as retained evidence, feature identity, architecture, safety, or authority.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260830220254-9113 — A provisional feature inventory is an evidence-bounded stakeholder adjudication surface [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824201733-0963 — Bounded provisional feature inventory v0.1 classifies 15 cross-product challenge cases [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824205433-1035 — Coverage-bounded provisional feature inventory v0.2 accounts for 33 three-product candidates [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824191243-1140 — A versioned provisional feature identity rule classifies three products while preserving correction lineage [possibly relevant]\n- 20260825163852-0028 — The 33-candidate provisional inventory is ready for a bounded evidence-tier view [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791904778889},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:19:38.890Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
