75bzYpkoOY87zqb2-GRlKiPKy0-JYvbSrFxf5ykoUDkHk4Ksge9LwhgeH68L4vfUvN9q3cLjXU-OBCdX_Y_Z6P6wbwpiolHgpOayAS0Wsb_gdD1mlq9BMs0vSSyiMW8tjn5YzlG2M6iE5ZC3FHQfxyRYGKW02aSva0ijX9KkX1nUv3UqvvZNYRACBhXstxyOpwrtJi9xZt4meDKlvlA5Z9k4k=\"}"},{"type":"text","text":"The skill’s controlling boundary is: “Mechanical preparation cannot accept feature identity,” and it requires exact reconciliation while preserving `UNKNOWN` and ambiguity. I’ll apply that ceiling and load the independent-adjudication guidance. The suggested notebook notes concern unrelated feature inventories, so: `skip-related: 20260830220254-9113 20260824201733-0963 20260824205433-1035 20260824191243-1140 20260825163852-0028 — this review concerns ADR0011 custody-contract evidence, not product feature identity.`","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03201568652b0503016ace4c0dd728819bb32e445394d0d9d3\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e0cf04034e2a42bebfb4ee59befeaa4e|fc_03201568652b0503016ace4c0f8870819bbea881338df124a3","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn read /Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace/.pi/skills/lsp-trace-feature-inventory/references/adjudication-and-acceptance.md","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1091,"output":201,"cacheRead":38272,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":20,"totalTokens":39564,"cost":{"input":0.004364,"output":0.00402,"cacheRead":0.015308800000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0236928}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791904778892,"responseId":"resp_03201568652b0503016ace4c0b2d54819b86fdade22829140e","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"minimal"},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:19:44.513Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"1f290c50-b945-4fe","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e0cf04034e2a42bebfb4ee59befeaa4e|fc_03201568652b0503016ace4c0f8870819bbea881338df124a3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Adjudication and acceptance\n2\t\n3\t## Independent semantic challenge\n4\t\n5\tA reviewer or separate review pass challenges the grouping without inheriting its conclusions. Independence is a relationship, not a required person, agent, or tool.\n6\t\n7\tCheck for:\n8\t\n9\t- unsupported merge or split conclusions;\n10\t- transitive paths treated as direct support;\n11\t- union evidence attributed to one seed;\n12\t- dispatch, sibling, community, centrality, or instability evidence treated as CALLS or feature semantics;\n13\t- successful bounded traversal treated as source completeness;\n14\t- bounded zero, `UNKNOWN`, failed, or successful-empty states treated as absence;\n15\t- capture-set composition treated as cross-capture CALLS or native custody;\n16\t- technical structure promoted into identity, purpose, value, production use, confidence, coverage, or acceptance;\n17\t- missing alternatives, falsifiers, or correction lineage;\n18\t- untouched ambiguity silently resolved.\n19\t\n20\tPreserve supported disagreement. A challenge can narrow, split, withdraw, or leave a hypothesis unresolved; it cannot manufacture missing authority.\n21\t\n22\t## Stakeholder correction\n23\t\n24\tProduct/domain stakeholders may admit semantic propositions under an explicit external authority. Record who/what supplied the correction, its scope, date/revision, affected candidate IDs, predecessors, and finite `inventory_state_delta`. Keep the underlying technical evidence unchanged.\n25\t\n26\tCorrections may rename, merge, split, exclude, or retain candidates. Do not erase prior revisions or unresolved alternatives. A stakeholder label does not retroactively authenticate source, execution, or technical coverage.\n27\t\n28\tIf stakeholder authority is unavailable or disputed, set `EXTERNAL_ADJUDICATION` or `UNRESOLVED`; do not guess. Untouched ambiguity remains explicit in the next revision.\n29\t\n30\t## Accepted-inventory boundary\n31\t\n32\tAn inventory is accepted only when a named external acceptance contract defines:\n33\t\n34\t- authorized decision-maker or admitted source;\n35\t- accepted scope and revision;\n36\t- proposition types being accepted;\n37\t- treatment of unresolved and excluded candidates;\n38\t- correction/reopening procedure;\n39\t- explicit coverage ceiling;\n40\t- acceptance record linked to candidate revisions.\n41\t\n42\tTechnical tools never satisfy this contract on their own. `ACCEPT_BOUNDARY` means a known evidence/scope boundary was consciously retained; it is not accepted feature identity. If no acceptance contract exists, report the inventory as provisional or unresolved.\n43\t\n44\t## Iterate under explicit bounds\n45\t\n46\tAcquire more evidence only for a named unresolved question with a proposed method/seed, expected discriminating result, explicit resource bounds, authority ceiling, and stop condition. Retain each round.\n47\t\n48\tAfter two consecutive rounds yield no new admissible evidence reference, changed disposition, narrowed alternative, or justified acquisition, the review may stop as `BOUNDED_REVIEW_DRY`. This is a workflow terminal, not complete feature or source coverage.\n49\t\n50\t## Human review view\n51\t\n52\tPrefer one row per candidate:\n53\t\n54\t```text\n55\tID | Working label | Status | Seeds | Evidence | Alternatives | Gaps | Revision\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\tLink to details containing exact references, failures, boundaries, competing interpretations, corrections, and acceptance authority. Lead with provisional capability and a public-safe explanation; make exact records and receipts optional audit detail.\n59\t\n60\tAttach examples and relationships only through exact stable joins and a stated bounded selection rule. If no exact relationship is established, say `not established`. Broader product/source evidence stays at its broader scope.\n61\t\n62\tNavigation groups, ordering, layout, proximity, color, communities, and visual density do not alter identity or status. Keep ungrouped candidates visible. Zero assignments to a group is an assignment state, not evidence of no capabilities.\n63\t\n64\tPlace unresolved merge/split questions next to affected candidates with evidence for each interpretation, blocking unknowns, and correction-safe consequences. Presentation improves comprehension only; any semantic regrouping requires an explicit revision and lineage.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260830220254-9113 — A provisional feature inventory is an evidence-bounded stakeholder adjudication surface [possibly relevant]\n- 20261007160414-2844 — DASL uses N/A as an explicit system- or user-applied data state [possibly relevant]\n- 20260909180258-8775 — Which May 2026 assessment proposals were accepted, superseded, or only exploratory? [possibly relevant]\n- 20260814163906-4069 — The retained EASI guide does not define row-count, checksum, semantic, or rollback acceptance checks. [possibly relevant]\n- 20260823224401-2998 — NAIS issue-resolution orientation stops until external or authentic evidence is reachable [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791904784512},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:19:44.513Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
