 enumeration from an exact committed implementation source manifest, source-derived actual IDs, independent `NECESSARY|REUSE|FALSE_POSITIVE|UNRESOLVED` classification, and `UNRESOLVED=0` before any later implementation GO;\n17\t7. planned-to-actual lineage handles realized, disappeared, split, merged, and emergent rows without reusing planned IDs;\n18\t8. source and run checksums verify and generated outputs reproduce byte-for-byte;\n19\t9. interface GO, RED GO, implementation GO, production admission, activation, and commit authority all remain false.\n20\t\n21\tRecord reviewer identity/revision, source-manifest result, run-manifest digest, reconciliation/count result, Stage A schema/completeness result, Stage B and correction-lineage result, immutable-evidence result, and exact token or one blocker.\n22\t\n23\tThe token qualifies contract bytes only. It does not authorize implementation or tests.\n24\t\n25\tCurrent disposition: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20261007014731-1322 — Integration receipt: Implement and independently review ADR0011 C18 reached-stage precedence and exact-once custody in the persistent ADR0011 worktree [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010153748-5419 — Integration receipt: Produce and independently review the immutable consolidated ADR0011 Stage 7 audit [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001214518-6991 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte Stage-B T4 completed-STOP lease-retirement RED-to-GREEN implementation/result review [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# Two-stage enumeration and adjudication contract\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n4\t\n5\t## Stage A: PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\n6\t\n7\tStage A separates source-backed present observations from future architecture obligations.\n8\t\n9\t### Existing-source contract\n10\t\n11\tAn `EXISTING_SOURCE` row is admissible only for an exact current source locator in these bounded families:\n12\t\n13\t- `Manager` as the current accounting-domain owner;\n14\t- current C15 account type, creation, and lifetime;\n15\t- current lease reservation, alias, transfer, and release capability;\n16\t- current terminal cleanup;\n17\t- nearby lease/borrow APIs that are explicitly observed as lifetime-bound and not reusable.\n18\t\n19\tAllowed statuses are `EXISTING_OBSERVED` and `EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE`. These are observations, not `NECESSARY`, `REUSE`, future design approval, or proof that the current API satisfies the directional contract.\n20\t\n21\t### Planned-obligation contract\n22\t\n23\tA planned row has no source line or source hash. It must use exactly one status from:\n24\t\n25\t- `PLANNED_RESERVATION`\n26\t- `PLANNED_COPY`\n27\t- `PLANNED_ALIAS`\n28\t- `PLANNED_TRANSFER`\n29\t- `PLANNED_RELEASE`\n30\t\n31\tIt binds an exact proposed file, symbol, component, attempt/account/lease identity, terminal paths where applicable, and predecessor lineage. `NECESSARY`, `REUSE`, `FALSE_POSITIVE`, and source-semantic `UNRESOLVED` are forbidden in Stage A planned rows because implementation source does not exist.\n32\t\n33\t### Stage A completeness\n34\t\n35\t`PREIMPLEMENTATION_COMPLETE` requires all 48 legacy identities accounted, duplicates `0`, omissions `0`, all six components covered by reservation/copy/alias obligations, whole-acquisition transfer present, and terminal convergence release present. It says nothing about actual implementation source semantics.\n36\t\n37\t## Stage B: POST-IMPLEMENTATION\n38\t\n39\tStage B begins only from an exact committed implementation revision and canonical source manifest. It does not accept line-0, absent-source, or planned rows as actual rows.\n40\t\n41\tThe canonical actual row ID is:\n42\t\n43\t```text\n44\tsha256(\"adr0011.c15.two-stage.actual.v1\\0\" ||\n45\t       source_path || \"\\0\" || symbol || \"\\0\" || operation_kind || \"\\0\" ||\n46\t       component || \"\\0\" || backing_identity_rule)\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tA deterministic source enumerator must emit every actual reservation, owned copy, alias/borrow, transfer, release, accounting owner/account lifecycle, and terminal cleanup relationship in scope. Two runs from the same committed manifest must be byte-identical. Actual duplicates and omissions must be zero.\n50\t\n51\tA separate independent pass classifies each actual row as exactly:\n52\t\n53\t- `NECESSARY`\n54\t- `REUSE`\n55\t- `FALSE_POSITIVE`\n56\t- `UNRESOLVED`\n57\t\n58\tEvery non-`UNRESOLVED` classification requires exact source evidence, contrary evidence or a falsifier, adjudicator identity, and revision. `IMPLEMENTATION_GO` requires `UNRESOLVED=0`; this contract does not return or authorize that gate.\n59\t\n60\t## Correction lineage\n61\t\n62\tPlanned and actual namespaces never alias. `planned_predecessor_ids` records architecture lineage without determining actual identity.\n63\t\n64\t- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65\t- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66\t- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67\t- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row and must be justified or block GO.\n68\t- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69\t\n70\tSplit and merge records list every predecessor and successor; no row is silently overwritten. A disappeared obligation is not a source absence claim until the complete committed manifest and canonical enumeration establish it.\n71\t\n72\t## Gate boundary\n73\t\n74\tThe exact token `ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO` qualifies only this ordering and schema. Interface/RED work remains blocked until that token. Implementation remains separately blocked and is never authorized by Stage A completeness or this package.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260805185048-9754 — Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824234609-5129 — Five current-source observations renew three ScopeRationalization rows at evidence tier only [possibly relevant]\n- 20260831182029-0487 — Pinned source supports read-only cross-app status aggregation but not a canonical identity contract [possibly relevant]\n- 20260827162246-6425 — Post-exact24 orientation selects independent exact-two blocked-row source recovery [possibly relevant]\n- 20260805185115-4797 — Internal phase-one planning describes 1,440 fixed hours and six deliverables, not yet reconciled to an executed SOW [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t{\n2\t  \"authority\": 0,\n3\t  \"implementation_go\": false,\n4\t  \"interface_go\": false,\n5\t  \"legacy_adjudicator_duplicates\": 0,\n6\t  \"legacy_adjudicator_identity_count\": 48,\n7\t  \"legacy_all_48_accounted\": true,\n8\t  \"legacy_matched\": 47,\n9\t  \"legacy_omissions_after_reconciliation\": 0,\n10\t  \"legacy_omissions_before_correction\": 1,\n11\t  \"legacy_producer_duplicates\": 0,\n12\t  \"legacy_producer_identity_count\": 47,\n13\t  \"red_go\": false,\n14\t  \"stage_a_existing_source_rows\": 13,\n15\t  \"stage_a_planned_obligation_rows\": 20,\n16\t  \"stage_a_preimplementation_complete\": true,\n17\t  \"stage_a_unresolved_identity_accounting\": 0,\n18\t  \"stage_b_actual_rows\": 0,\n19\t  \"stage_b_implementation_go\": false,\n20\t  \"stage_b_unresolved\": null,\n21\t  \"status\": \"AUTHORED_NOT_GO\",\n22\t  \"target\": \"ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO\"\n23\t}\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260817144058-8772 — DASL's normal web submission writes status 9 while legacy statuses 6–9 display as Submitted [possibly relevant]\n- 20260729195634-7197 — NAIS requires remaining legacy solutions and interfaces to be retired. [possibly relevant]\n- 20260729201642-0162 — Axiom: Legacy retirement is an endpoint after migration coexistence, not a synonym for migration start. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010153748-5419 — Integration receipt: Produce and independently review the immutable consolidated ADR0011 Stage 7 audit [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Deterministic documentation-only producer for the ADR0011 C15 two-stage contract.\"\"\"\n3\timport csv\n4\timport hashlib\n5\timport json\n6\tfrom pathlib import Path\n7\t\n8\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n9\tOUT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n10\tHEAD = \"a1cd77950ffa45ebed52310878f772f3c7344756\"\n11\tV1 = ROOT / \"docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-enumeration-v1\"\n12\tTARGET = \"ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO\"\n13\tTERMINALS = \"normal|complete-empty|malformed|protocol|transport|unsupported|timeout|cancel|refusal|STOP|RESTART|Shutdown|stale-generation|race|duplicate-release\"\n14\t\n15\t\n16\tdef digest_bytes(data):\n17\t    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()\n18\t\n19\t\n20\tdef file_digest(path):\n21\t    return digest_bytes(path.read_bytes())\n22\t\n23\t\n24\tdef stable_id(namespace, *parts):\n25\t    return digest_bytes((namespace + \"\\0\" + \"\\0\".join(parts)).encode())\n26\t\n27\t\n28\tdef write_tsv(name, fields, rows):\n29\t    with (OUT / name).open(\"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n30\t        writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fields, delimiter=\"\\t\", lineterminator=\"\\n\")\n31\t        writer.writeheader()\n32\t        writer.writerows(rows)\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t# Preserve v1 as immutable negative evidence. The package is read, never rewritten.\n36\twith (V1 / \"UNRESOLVED.tsv\").open(newline=\"\") as f:\n37\t    producer_rows = list(csv.DictReader(f, delimiter=\"\\t\"))\n38\tif len(producer_rows) != 47 or len({r[\"row_id\"] for r in producer_rows}) != 47:\n39\t    raise SystemExit(\"expected exact immutable producer set: 47 unique rows\")\n40\t\n41\tmissing_symbol = \"reserveDirectionalComponentV2\"\n42\tmissing_component = \"ALL_SIX_COMPONENTS\"\n43\tmissing_id = stable_id(\n44\t    \"adr0011.c15.lease-source.v2.row\",\n45\t    \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\",\n46\t    missing_symbol,\n47\t    \"RESERVE\",\n48\t    missing_component,\n49\t    \"planned exact pre-effect component/bytes/attempt/account reservation\",\n50\t)\n51\t\n52\treconciliation = []\n53\tfor index, row in enumerate(sorted(producer_rows, key=lambda r: r[\"row_id\"]), 1):\n54\t    reconciliation.append({\n55\t        \"identity_ordinal\": str(index),\n56\t        \"adjudicator_identity\": row[\"row_id\"],\n57\t        \"producer_row_id\": row[\"row_id\"],\n58\t        \"source_path\": row[\"source_path\"],\n59\t        \"symbol\": row[\"symbol\"],\n60\t        \"operation_kind\": row[\"operation_kind\"],\n61\t        \"component\": row[\"component\"],\n62\t        \"reconciliation\": \"MATCHED_PRODUCER_ROW\",\n63\t        \"cause\": \"exact identity present in producer47\",\n64\t    })\n65\treconciliation.append({\n66\t    \"identity_ordinal\": \"48\",\n67\t    \"adjudicator_identity\": missing_id,\n68\t    \"producer_row_id\": \"\",\n69\t    \"source_path\": \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\",\n70\t    \"symbol\": missing_symbol,\n71\t    \"operation_kind\": \"RESERVE\",\n72\t    \"component\": missing_component,\n73\t    \"reconciliation\": \"OMITTED_BY_PRODUCER47\",\n74\t    \"cause\": \"generator iterated ALLOCATE and ALIAS plus one TRANSFER and RELEASE, but never emitted the architecture-required pre-effect RESERVE identity\",\n75\t})\n76\treconciliation.sort(key=lambda r: int(r[\"identity_ordinal\"]))\n77\twrite_tsv(\"LEGACY_48_IDENTITY_RECONCILIATION.tsv\", list(reconciliation[0]), reconciliation)\n78\t\n79\texisting_specs = [\n80\t    (\"sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go\", 1564, \"Manager\", \"ACCOUNTING_OWNER\", \"MANAGER_ACCOUNTING_DOMAIN\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current Manager owns the accounting-domain lock and lifecycle integration point\"),\n81\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 125, \"privateB4ByteAccountV2\", \"ACCOUNT_LIFETIME\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current versioned transaction account type\"),\n82\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 147, \"newPrivateB4ByteAccountV2\", \"ACCOUNT_CREATE\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account constructor\"),\n83\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 174, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).reserve\", \"LEASE_RESERVE\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current byte-lease reservation API\"),\n84\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 379, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).aliasPrivateB4C15\", \"LEASE_ALIAS\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account-local alias capability\"),\n85\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 495, \"(*privateB4ByteLeaseV2).Release\", \"LEASE_RELEASE\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current lease release API\"),\n86\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 557, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).transferDiagnosticBacking\", \"LEASE_TRANSFER\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current single diagnostic transfer capability\"),\n87\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 561, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).transferDiagnosticBackingPair\", \"LEASE_TRANSFER\", \"C15_LEASE_SET\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current paired diagnostic transfer capability\"),\n88\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 660, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).requestTerminalRelease\", \"TERMINAL_CLEANUP\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account terminal-release request\"),\n89\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 670, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).maybeReleaseBackingLocked\", \"TERMINAL_CLEANUP\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current terminal backing cleanup\"),\n90\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go\", 112, \"OwnedMethodPairLease.WithPair\", \"NONREUSABLE_BORROW\", \"NEARBY_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE\", \"nearby callback borrow is lifetime-bound and is not a reusable directional acquisition\"),\n91\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go\", 311, \"callHierarchyObservationLease.withObservation\", \"NONREUSABLE_BORROW\", \"NEARBY_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE\", \"nearby observation borrow is lifetime-bound and is not reusable\"),\n92\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go\", 639, \"callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease.Callback\", \"NONREUSABLE_BORROW\", \"NEARBY_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE\", \"nearby generic callback lease is synchronous and not reusable\"),\n93\t]\n94\texisting = []\n95\tfor path, line, symbol, kind, component, classification, observation in existing_specs:\n96\t    p = ROOT / path\n97\t    existing.append({\n98\t        \"stage_a_row_id\": stable_id(\"adr0011.c15.two-stage.stage-a.existing.v1\", path, symbol, kind, component),\n99\t        \"row_kind\": \"EXISTING_SOURCE\",\n100\t        \"status\": classification,\n101\t        \"source_path\": path,\n102\t        \"source_start_line\": str(line),\n103\t        \"source_end_line\": str(line),\n104\t        \"source_sha256\": file_digest(p),\n105\t        \"symbol\": symbol,\n106\t        \"operation_kind\": kind,\n107\t        \"component\": component,\n108\t        \"attempt_identity\": \"CURRENT_SOURCE_ONLY\",\n109\t        \"account_identity\": \"CURRENT_SOURCE_ONLY\",\n110\t        \"lease_identity\": \"CURRENT_SOURCE_ONLY\",\n111\t        \"terminal_paths\": TERMINALS if kind == \"TERMINAL_CLEANUP\" else \"\",\n112\t        \"predecessor_lineage\": \"NULL@0\",\n113\t        \"obligation\": observation,\n114\t        \"authority_ceiling\": \"SOURCE_OBSERVATION_ONLY; no future necessity or reuse conclusion\",\n115\t    })\n116\twrite_tsv(\"STAGE_A_EXISTING_SOURCE.tsv\", list(existing[0]), existing)\n117\t\n118\tplanned_specs = []\n119\tcomponents = [\"PREPARE_FRAME\", \"PREPARE_RESULT\", \"SELECTED_HANDOFF\", \"DIRECTIONAL_FRAME\", \"DIRECTIONAL_RESULT\", \"RETAINED_EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE\"]\n120\tfor component in components:\n121\t    key = component.lower()\n122\t    planned_specs.append((f\"reserveDirectional{component.title().replace('_','')}V3\", \"PLANNED_RESERVATION\", component, f\"attempt_id+account_id+{component}+exact_bytes\", \"none\", \"reserve before owned effect\"))\n123\t    planned_specs.append((f\"copyDirectional{component.title().replace('_','')}V3\", \"PLANNED_COPY\", component, f\"attempt_id+account_id+{component}+backing_id\", \"reservation row for same component\", \"owned bytes and all leases remain inseparable\"))\n124\t    planned_specs.append((f\"aliasDirectional{component.title().replace('_','')}V3\", \"PLANNED_ALIAS\", component, f\"attempt_id+account_id+{component}+owner_lease_id+offset+length\", \"copy or transferred owner for same component\", \"zero-charge bounded alias; no escape or independent publication\"))\n125\tplanned_specs.append((\"transferDirectionalAcquisitionV3\", \"PLANNED_TRANSFER\", \"ALL_SIX_COMPONENTS\", \"source_attempt+destination_attempt+source_account+destination_account+complete_lease_set\", \"reservation/copy/alias rows for transferred acquisition\", \"atomically move complete bytes plus leases; preserve source on failure\"))\n126\tplanned_specs.append((\"releaseDirectionalTerminalV3\", \"PLANNED_RELEASE\", \"ALL_SIX_COMPONENTS\", \"attempt_id+account_id+all_active_lease_ids+release_id\", \"all rows for the attempt\", \"one terminal winner clears aliases/bytes and releases every lease exactly once\"))\n127\tplanned = []\n128\tfor symbol, status, component, identity, predecessor, obligation in planned_specs:\n129\t    planned.append({\n130\t        \"stage_a_row_id\": stable_id(\"adr0011.c15.two-stage.stage-a.planned.v1\", \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\", symbol, status, component, identity),\n131\t        \"row_kind\": \"PLANNED_OBLIGATION\",\n132\t        \"status\": status,\n133\t        \"proposed_source_path\": \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\",\n134\t        \"proposed_symbol\": symbol,\n135\t        \"component\": component,\n136\t        \"attempt_account_lease_identity\": identity,\n137\t        \"terminal_paths\": TERMINALS if status == \"PLANNED_RELEASE\" else \"\",\n138\t        \"predecessor_lineage\": predecessor,\n139\t        \"obligation\": obligation,\n140\t        \"source_semantics\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE_PREIMPLEMENTATION\",\n141\t        \"authority_ceiling\": \"PLANNED_ARCHITECTURE_OBLIGATION_ONLY; no NECESSARY/REUSE classification\",\n142\t    })\n143\twrite_tsv(\"STAGE_A_PLANNED_OBLIGATIONS.tsv\", list(planned[0]), planned)\n144\t\n145\tstage_b_fields = [\"actual_row_id\", \"source_path\", \"source_start_line\", \"source_end_line\", \"source_sha256\", \"symbol\", \"operation_kind\", \"component\", \"attempt_identity\", \"account_identity\", \"lease_identity\", \"classification\", \"planned_predecessor_ids\", \"lineage_event\", \"contrary_evidence\", \"adjudicator_id\", \"adjudication_revision\"]\n146\twrite_tsv(\"STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv\", stage_b_fields, [])\n147\t\n148\tcounts = {\n149\t    \"target\": TARGET,\n150\t    \"status\": \"AUTHORED_NOT_GO\",\n151\t    \"legacy_adjudicator_identity_count\": 48,\n152\t    \"legacy_producer_identity_count\": 47,\n153\t    \"legacy_matched\": 47,\n154\t    \"legacy_producer_duplicates\": 0,\n155\t    \"legacy_adjudicator_duplicates\": 0,\n156\t    \"legacy_omissions_before_correction\": 1,\n157\t    \"legacy_omissions_after_reconciliation\": 0,\n158\t    \"legacy_all_48_accounted\": True,\n159\t    \"stage_a_existing_source_rows\": len(existing),\n160\t    \"stage_a_planned_obligation_rows\": len(planned),\n161\t    \"stage_a_unresolved_identity_accounting\": 0,\n162\t    \"stage_a_preimplementation_complete\": True,\n163\t    \"stage_b_actual_rows\": 0,\n164\t    \"stage_b_unresolved\": None,\n165\t    \"stage_b_implementation_go\": False,\n166\t    \"interface_go\": False,\n167\t    \"red_go\": False,\n168\t    \"implementation_go\": False,\n169\t    \"authority\": 0,\n170\t}\n171\t(OUT / \"COUNTS.json\").write_text(json.dumps(counts, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n172\t\n173\tsource_paths = sorted({r[\"source_path\"] for r in existing})\n174\twith (OUT / \"SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256\").open(\"w\") as f:\n175\t    f.write(f\"# HEAD {HEAD}\\n\")\n176\t    for path in source_paths:\n177\t        p = ROOT / path\n178\t        f.write(f\"{file_digest(p)}  {p.stat().st_size}  {path}\\n\")\n179\t    for name in [\"UNRESOLVED.tsv\", \"COUNTS.json\", \"RUN_MANIFEST.sha256\", \"generate.py\"]:\n180\t        p = V1 / name\n181\t        f.write(f\"{file_digest(p)}  {p.stat().st_size}  docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-enumeration-v1/{name}\\n\")\n182\t\n183\tfiles = sorted(p for p in OUT.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name != \"RUN_MANIFEST.sha256\")\n184\twith (OUT / \"RUN_MANIFEST.sha256\").open(\"w\") as f:\n185\t    for p in files:\n186\t        f.write(f\"{file_digest(p)}  {p.name}\\n\")\n187\tprint(json.dumps(counts, sort_keys=True))\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005192502-3026 — Integration receipt: Independently review complete ADR0011 C15 private transaction accounting production migration to V2 account/lease family [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006014845-6698 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial retained-notification lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, refusal atomicity, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261004230052-1374 — Integration receipt: Independently adjudicate bounded ADR0011 C15 custodial private-B4 ingress params-copy accounting [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824234609-5129 — Five current-source observations renew three ScopeRationalization rows at evidence tier only [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n\n[Showing lines 305-977 of 977 (50.0KB limit). Full output: /var/folders/bc/qbdy42vs4jn56zwrb2y09l9m0000gn/T/pi-bash-a8e2e91509154ec6.log]"}],"details":{"truncation":{"content":"128\t```\n129\t\n130\t## Independent adjudication\n131\t\n132\tA separate review pass, identified in each row by `adjudicator_id` and `adjudication_revision`, reviews source bytes without inheriting mechanical classifications. It challenges hidden copies, alias escape, lease mismatch, transfer partiality, release gaps, row merges/splits, transitive assumptions, baseline carry-forward, and bounded-zero/absence claims. Independence is a review relationship; no delegation is required.\n133\t\n134\tEvery non-`UNRESOLVED` row requires contrary evidence or a falsifier. Corrections create a new monotonically increasing row revision with exact `predecessor_row_id` and `predecessor_revision`, verified canonical revision hash, and finite delta; native source evidence is never rewritten. The independent pass rejects cycles, missing predecessors, branches, duplicate tips, and unjustified split/merge continuity or leaves them `UNRESOLVED`. Structural adjacency, names, CALLS, or generated registry membership cannot accept identity.\n135\t\n136\tGate prerequisites:\n137\t\n138\t- both deterministic mechanical runs match;\n139\t- all manifests/checksums verify;\n140\t- every source candidate and baseline identity reconciles;\n141\t- every allocation/release/borrow/transfer site is adjudicated;\n142\t- `UNRESOLVED.tsv` exists with header only and `UNRESOLVED=0` in counts;\n143\t- no write-set expansion or architecture hard stop;\n144\t- independent reviewer returns the exact gate for this package checksum.\n145\t\n146\tUntil then disposition remains `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260821193348-8201 — Current-source access orientation selects a six-repository predecessor-impact envelope [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824234609-5129 — Five current-source observations renew three ScopeRationalization rows at evidence tier only [possibly relevant]\n- 20260814163906-4069 — The retained EASI guide does not define row-count, checksum, semantic, or rollback acceptance checks. [possibly relevant]\n- 20260827162246-6425 — Post-exact24 orientation selects independent exact-two blocked-row source recovery [possibly relevant]\n- 20260826200941-1958 — Post-row-21 completion orientation selects row-1 metadata candidate-gap adjudication [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# Successor impact on private interface v2\n2\t\n3\tStatus: design contract only; not a compile contract and not permission to edit immutable v2.\n4\t\n5\t## Required successor types\n6\t\n7\tA later interface v3 (or other explicitly reviewed successor) must express at least:\n8\t\n9\t```go\n10\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2 uint64\n11\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseIDV2 uint64\n12\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalTransferIDV2 uint64\n13\t\n14\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountV2 struct {\n15\t    ID privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2\n16\t    Attempt privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAttemptIDV1\n17\t    Direction privateCallHierarchyDirectionV1\n18\t    LiveBytes, ReservedBytes uint64\n19\t    State privateCallHierarchyDirectionalStateV1\n20\t    Components [6]privateCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentAccountV2\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseV2 struct {\n24\t    ID privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseIDV2\n25\t    Account privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2\n26\t    Attempt privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAttemptIDV1\n27\t    Component privateCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentV1\n28\t    Capacity uint64\n29\t    Active bool\n30\t    BackingID uint64\n31\t}\n32\t\n33\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAliasV2 struct {\n34\t    OwnerLease privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseIDV2\n35\t    Offset, Length uint64\n36\t}\n37\t\n38\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAcquisitionV2 struct {\n39\t    Account privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2\n40\t    Attempt privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAttemptIDV1\n41\t    Component privateCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentV1\n42\t    Bytes []byte\n43\t    Capacity uint64\n44\t    Leases []privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseV2\n45\t    Alias *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAliasV2\n46\t    Valid bool\n47\t}\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\tNames are architecture identifiers only. A successor interface must independently prove package typing and may refine representation without weakening the invariants.\n51\t\n52\t## Required successor signatures\n53\t\n54\t```go\n55\treserveDirectionalComponentV2(account, attempt, component, bytes) (reservation, stage, reason)\n56\tacquireDirectionalOwnedV2(reservation, source) (acquisition, stage, reason, error)\n57\tdeclareDirectionalAliasV2(ownerAcquisition, component, offset, length) (acquisition, stage, reason)\n58\ttransferDirectionalAcquisitionV2(source *acquisition, destination) (transferID, destinationAcquisition, stage, reason)\n59\tborrowDirectionalV2(acquisition, fn) error\n60\tpublishDirectionalV2(acquisition, destination) (receipt, stage, reason)\n61\treleaseDirectionalTerminalV2(account, terminal) bool\n62\t```\n63\t\n64\tThe successor lock contract is exact: any nested account operation uses `Manager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu -> privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu` and releases in reverse order. Account-local entrypoints must never acquire owner or Manager locks while holding `privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu`; they return/retry through a Manager-owned entrypoint after dropping the account lock. Terminal release is the sole nested-discharge coordinator and uses a non-callback account primitive.\n65\t\n66\tContract requirements:\n67\t\n68\t- reserve identifies exact component/bytes/attempt/account and precedes every owned copy/effect;\n69\t- owned acquisition creates or receives bytes only together with corresponding active leases;\n70\t- alias declaration creates no lease/charge and binds to one owning lease range;\n71\t- transfer consumes the complete source handle atomically and never accepts detached `raw []byte` plus detached lease;\n72\t- borrow cannot retain or return bytes;\n73\t- publication requires a still-valid acquisition and cannot create an uncharged retained copy;\n74\t- release is the sole convergence point;\n75\t- reserve, alias, transfer, ordinary release, and terminal release expose no callback or reverse-lock path from the account;\n76\t- terminal release invalidates aliases/bytes and discharges leases/account counters atomically under the complete order.\n77\t\n78\t## Exact v2 corrections\n79\t\n80\tImmutable v2 must not be edited. Its successor must change these design-level contracts:\n81\t\n82\t| v2 contract | successor requirement |\n83\t|---|---|\n84\t| transfer accepts detached raw bytes and one `*privateB4ByteLeaseV2` | transfer accepts one lease-bearing acquisition containing all bytes and corresponding leases |\n85\t| custody metadata owns neither bytes nor lease | acquisition is the non-escapable lifetime handle for bytes plus leases (or bounded alias) |\n86\t| seven generic component slots | six exhaustive charged component classes; aliases are rows bound to owners, not charged slots |\n87\t| validation can occur after caller has raw bytes | reservation and acquisition occur before every owned copy/effect |\n88\t| one moved charge is sufficient | lease set must correspond exactly to all retained owned capacities |\n89\t\n90\tNo claim is made that these declarations compile against current source. This is sufficient design detail for a later separately reviewed interface update only. A successor must reject account-first, owner-first-then-Manager, post-unlock discharge, account callback, try-lock/timeout/asynchronous discharge, and duplicate owner/account/terminal alternatives.\n91\t\n92\t## Frozen compatibility and authority\n93\t\n94\tThe successor must preserve generic provider-neutral profile identity, independent incoming/outgoing contracts, sole owner/terminal, exact terminal distinctions, target-set accounting, no-history-change, disabled/`CALLS_ONLY` value equality, authority `0`, default off, `CALLS_ONLY`, and unchanged Definition/Reference behavior. It cannot import Go/gopls semantics into the generic interface.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006021001-8737 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial matched ServerError lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, consumer non-escape, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006014845-6698 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial retained-notification lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, refusal atomicity, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005192502-3026 — Integration receipt: Independently review complete ADR0011 C15 private transaction accounting production migration to V2 account/lease family [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006023814-5955 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial unmatched/late retained-response lease accounting, transactional publication, lifecycle joining, and callback non-escape. [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# ADR0011 directional raw-custody C15 lease-source v2 qualification package\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`  \n4\tExact requested gate: `ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_LEASE_SOURCE_V2_GO`  \n5\tSource HEAD: `162d796f7e33fea2c2bdb98f92e41744bb728c2d`  \n6\tAuthority: `0`; accepted: `false`; defaults: unchanged/off; relation authority: `CALLS_ONLY`; Definition/Reference: unchanged.\n7\t\n8\tThis is a documentation-only, versioned architecture qualification package. It authorizes no implementation, production/test mutation, execution, evidence mutation, profile activation, public API/schema/configuration/registry/build-tag change, deployment, commit, or admission.\n9\t\n10\t## Decision frozen here\n11\t\n12\tOne dedicated directional-raw subledger is added conceptually inside the existing `Manager` accounting domain. It is metadata and lease coordination, not a second recorder, backing owner, terminal owner, C15 account, or source of capacity. Every owned copy is preceded by an exact reservation for component, bytes, attempt, and account. Every acquisition result carries the exact bytes and corresponding leases; bytes cannot escape that result. Aliases are zero-charge bounded views tied to an owning lease. Transfer moves bytes and lease atomically, invalidating both at source only on success. Every terminal and race converges on one exact release.\n13\t\n14\tThe package also freezes a correction-safe C15 current-source enumeration plan. Counts are not mechanically enumerated here and are therefore deliberately absent, provisional, and non-authoritative. `UNRESOLVED=0` is required before the requested gate can be returned.\n15\t\n16\t## Immutable blocked evidence\n17\t\n18\tThe following remain byte-identical blocked predecessors and are not modified, adopted as sufficient, or granted authority:\n19\t\n20\t- generic profile amendment package, `SHA256SUMS` digest `df44a8befc36ff69b7e903be2b78b5cf9fbb508538b8cf04ed5bbb7fd35b2df7`;\n21\t- private interface v1, `SHA256SUMS` digest `d36211da45adb55e83f0b112a62140d7bec5ef2076edee12c3facebbd692af7c`;\n22\t- private interface v2, `SHA256SUMS` digest `8f329e1012278a7e92220d0499047a7b486402fcc2db8d10f7b4b2dcb06feeda`.\n23\t\n24\tTheir blocker is retained: v1/v2 accept detached raw bytes plus one caller-held lease and permit custody metadata that does not itself carry all corresponding leases. They therefore do not prove lease-source closure for every owned component and cannot satisfy this gate.\n25\t\n26\t## Normative order\n27\t\n28\t1. `ARCHITECTURE.md`\n29\t2. `INTERFACE_V2_IMPACT.md`\n30\t3. `C15_ENUMERATION_PLAN.md`\n31\t4. `WRITESET.md`\n32\t5. `SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256`\n33\t6. `REVIEW_REQUEST.md`\n34\t7. `SHA256SUMS`\n35\t\n36\tAny required write-set expansion, public/global/default change, second owner/terminal/account, uncharged owned copy, byte reconstruction, lease-free escape, non-atomic transfer, unresolved census row, or changed D/R/CALLS authority is a hard stop.\n37\t\n38\tAUTHORED_NOT_GO\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261006023814-5955 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial unmatched/late retained-response lease accounting, transactional publication, lifecycle joining, and callback non-escape. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005192502-3026 — Integration receipt: Independently review complete ADR0011 C15 private transaction accounting production migration to V2 account/lease family [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006021001-8737 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial matched ServerError lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, consumer non-escape, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006014845-6698 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial retained-notification lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, refusal atomicity, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# Independent architecture qualification review request\n2\t\n3\tReview exact package bytes at source HEAD `162d796f7e33fea2c2bdb98f92e41744bb728c2d`.\n4\t\n5\t## Requested token\n6\t\n7\tReturn exactly:\n8\t\n9\t`ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_LEASE_SOURCE_V2_GO`\n10\t\n11\tonly if every condition below is satisfied for the final `SHA256SUMS`:\n12\t\n13\t- one Manager-domain directional-raw subledger; no second recorder/owner/terminal/account;\n14\t- exhaustive six-component charge table and zero-charge aliases bound to owning leases;\n15\t- reservation before every owned copy/effect with exact component/bytes/attempt/account and +1 refusal accounting;\n16\t- acquisition results inseparably carry bytes and all corresponding leases; no escape;\n17\t- transfer atomically moves bytes+leases, invalidating source only on success and preserving exactly one source owner on failure;\n18\t- complete nested order is exactly `Manager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu -> privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu`, reverse/account-held upward acquisition is prohibited, rejected alternatives are explicit, and terminal nested discharge is atomic;\n19\t- every terminal/race converges on exact-once release with no double/orphan;\n20\t- existing frozen tests plan terminal release races/deadlock checks against account reserve, alias, transfer, and ordinary release without write-set expansion;\n21\t- explicit copy/alias/borrow/transfer policy forbids reconstruction and uncharged retained copies;\n22\t- correction-safe current-source C15 enumeration has deterministic manifests, stable rows, exact predecessor lineage/revision hashes, genesis sentinel, monotonic revisions, cycle/missing-predecessor/branch handling, independent adjudication, and requires `UNRESOLVED=0` without claiming unrun final counts;\n23\t- private interface v1/v2 and generic amendment remain immutable blocked evidence;\n24\t- production/test impact remains exactly six plus four, with hard stop on expansion;\n25\t- authority remains `0`, accepted remains false, defaults remain off, relation authority remains `CALLS_ONLY`, and Definition/Reference behavior is unchanged.\n26\t\n27\t## Review outputs\n28\t\n29\tRecord:\n30\t\n31\t1. reviewer identity and review revision;\n32\t2. package `SHA256SUMS` digest;\n33\t3. source-manifest verification;\n34\t4. invariant-by-invariant result;\n35\t5. write-set boundary result;\n36\t6. blocker-evidence immutability result;\n37\t7. complete lock-order, rejected-alternative, and terminal-discharge result;\n38\t8. planned race/deadlock obligation and no-expansion result;\n39\t9. C15 lineage and correction-safety result;\n40\t10. exact token or one precise blocker.\n41\t\n42\tThis token qualifies architecture bytes only. It is not implementation GO, RED/test GO, enumeration execution GO, profile/provider GO, activation, admission, commit, or production authority. Even after token issuance, mechanical enumeration and a separately reviewed successor interface remain required before any later implementation request.\n43\t\n44\tCurrent disposition: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006235523-4470 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only DESIGN_GO review of ADR0011 C18 owner and write-set proposal [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001161357-2332 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte result review of frozen ADR0011 A11 disposable guard V3 execution-v1 [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001214518-6991 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte Stage-B T4 completed-STOP lease-retirement RED-to-GREEN implementation/result review [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006211618-9893 — Integration receipt: Independently adjudicate revised ADR0011 C17 acquisition provisional-token design and exact production write set [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# Exact immutable future write-set\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`. This package changes none of these production/test files.\n4\t\n5\t## Production: exactly six\n6\t\n7\t1. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go` — required-new private mechanics; successor lease-bearing acquisition/account/alias/transfer declarations.\n8\t2. `sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go` — one Manager subledger; reserve-before-effect integration and terminal convergence under existing lock.\n9\t3. `internal/lspwire/read_frame.go` — private bounded acquisition result carrying bytes with corresponding lease source; defaults unchanged.\n10\t4. `internal/lspwire/successor_ingress.go` — conditional already-reserved bound and acquisition threading only; byte-identical if unused.\n11\t5. `sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go` — sole direction-neutral owner/terminal integration, atomic acquisition transfer, alias invalidation, exact release.\n12\t6. `sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go` — generated only from accepted `UNRESOLVED=0` enumeration; never hand-edited.\n13\t\n14\t## Tests: exactly four new files\n15\t\n16\t1. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private_test.go`.\n17\t2. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_race_private_test.go`.\n18\t3. `internal/lspwire/read_frame_bounded_incomplete_v1_private_test.go`.\n19\t4. `internal/lspwire/successor_ingress_directional_v1_private_test.go`.\n20\t\n21\tThe existing selector/package ownership remains unchanged. Future tests must additionally prove every component reservation tuple, lease-bearing no-escape acquisition, zero-charge alias lifetime, atomic bytes+lease transfer in both success/failure, every terminal/race release convergence, no double/orphan, and exact C15 delta reconciliation.\n22\t\n23\tWithout adding files, `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_race_private_test.go` owns planned adversarial schedules for terminal release versus account reserve, alias declaration/use, acquisition transfer, and ordinary account/lease release. Each schedule must prove the only nested order is `Manager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu -> privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu`, account-held paths never acquire owner/Manager, one terminal winner, bounded completion without deadlock/livelock, exact counter/lease/alias postconditions, and duplicate losers as no-op. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private_test.go` owns deterministic lock-contract/refusal and terminal-discharge postconditions. The two existing `internal/lspwire` test files remain transport-only and must not fabricate account locking. These are planned obligations only; no test is created or run here.\n24\t\n25\t## Hard stop\n26\t\n27\tThere is no fallback or expansion. If any architecture, interface, RED, implementation, enumeration, generation, compatibility, or release obligation requires an unlisted production/test path, historical test/fixture/corpus/golden mutation, public surface, dependency, schema/profile/registry/config/build-tag/package-boundary change, the exact disposition is:\n28\t\n29\t`BLOCKED_WRITESET_EXPANSION_REQUIRED`\n30\t\n31\tNo implementation or test mutation may proceed under this package.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261006235523-4470 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only DESIGN_GO review of ADR0011 C18 owner and write-set proposal [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261004222557-4857 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only integration review of ADR0011 C15 private-B4 returned request-frame ownership via bounded caller lease [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# ADR0011 directional-raw custody C15 two-stage contract v2\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`  \n4\tTarget review token: `ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO`  \n5\tSource HEAD: `a1cd77950ffa45ebed52310878f772f3c7344756`  \n6\tAuthority: `0`; accepted: `false`; implementation authority: `none`.\n7\t\n8\tThis documentation-only successor corrects the gate ordering of `adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-enumeration-v1` without modifying it. The v1 package, including its `UNRESOLVED.tsv`, result, counts, generator, and run manifest, remains immutable negative evidence. Its absent-source rows are not normalized, overwritten, or semantically classified here.\n9\t\n10\t## Mechanical 47/48 reconciliation\n11\t\n12\tThe v1 producer emitted 47 unique rows: 33 current-source candidates and 14 absent-successor proposals. The independently supplied adjudication denominator was 48. `LEGACY_48_IDENTITY_RECONCILIATION.tsv` accounts for all exact identities. Forty-seven match the exact producer row IDs. Identity 48 is the omitted planned `reserveDirectionalComponentV2` obligation. The cause is mechanical: v1 `generate.py` iterates six `ALLOCATE` and six `ALIAS` proposals and appends one `TRANSFER` and one `RELEASE`, but never emits the architecture/interface-required pre-effect reservation operation. Reconciliation therefore reports producer duplicates `0`, adjudicator duplicates `0`, post-reconciliation omissions `0`, and all 48 accounted.\n13\t\n14\tThis correction does not infer source semantics for the absent proposed file. The omitted identity is a planned obligation only.\n15\t\n16\t## Two stages\n17\t\n18\t### Stage A — PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\n19\t\n20\t`STAGE_A_EXISTING_SOURCE.tsv` contains only narrow current-source observations for the Manager accounting owner, account creation/lifetime, lease reserve/alias/release and transfer capabilities, terminal cleanup, and nearby lifetime-bound nonreusable borrows. Its only classifications are `EXISTING_OBSERVED` and `EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE`; neither means future necessity or reuse approval.\n21\t\n22\t`STAGE_A_PLANNED_OBLIGATIONS.tsv` contains exact future obligations only. Each row is one of `PLANNED_RESERVATION`, `PLANNED_COPY`, `PLANNED_ALIAS`, `PLANNED_TRANSFER`, or `PLANNED_RELEASE`, with proposed file, symbol, component, attempt/account/lease identity, terminal paths where applicable, and predecessor lineage. Stage A contains no `NECESSARY` or `REUSE` classification.\n23\t\n24\tStage A completeness means:\n25\t\n26\t1. all 48 legacy identities are mechanically accounted with duplicates and omissions equal to zero;\n27\t2. every architecture component has exact planned reservation, copy, and alias obligations;\n28\t3. whole-acquisition transfer and terminal release obligations are present;\n29\t4. current-source observations stay narrow and source-backed;\n30\t5. no absent source is semantically classified.\n31\t\n32\tStage A completeness is architecture-obligation completeness, not source-semantic completeness and not implementation GO.\n33\t\n34\t### Stage B — POST-IMPLEMENTATION\n35\t\n36\tAfter an implementation is separately authorized and committed, a canonical source enumerator must regenerate actual rows from an exact committed implementation source manifest. Actual row IDs are source-derived and must not reuse planned IDs. `STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv` is intentionally header-only before implementation.\n37\t\n38\tAn independent review then classifies every actual row as exactly `NECESSARY`, `REUSE`, `FALSE_POSITIVE`, or `UNRESOLVED`. `UNRESOLVED=0`, exact source-manifest verification, deterministic duplicate/omission checks, and complete planned-to-actual correction lineage are required before any later `IMPLEMENTATION_GO` can be considered.\n39\t\n40\tPlanned-to-actual lineage is many-to-many and correction-safe: disappeared plans are recorded as `DISAPPEARED`; one plan producing several actual rows is `SPLIT`; several plans producing one actual row is `MERGED`; ordinary correspondence is `REALIZED`. Actual identities always derive from committed source path, symbol, operation, component, and backing identity. Planned IDs remain predecessors/evidence and never become actual row IDs.\n41\t\n42\t## Gate ordering\n43\t\n44\tThe requested two-stage token qualifies these contract bytes only. It is not interface GO, RED/test GO, implementation GO, production admission, activation, commit authority, or permission to mutate production/tests. Interface and RED remain blocked until the two-stage contract receives its exact review token. Implementation remains blocked until separately authorized after interface and RED gates. Stage B cannot run until a committed implementation exists, and this package does not authorize creating one.\n45\t\n46\tNormative order:\n47\t\n48\t1. `TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT.md`\n49\t2. `LEGACY_48_IDENTITY_RECONCILIATION.tsv`\n50\t3. `STAGE_A_EXISTING_SOURCE.tsv`\n51\t4. `STAGE_A_PLANNED_OBLIGATIONS.tsv`\n52\t5. `STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv`\n53\t6. `COUNTS.json`\n54\t7. `SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256`\n55\t8. `REVIEW_REQUEST.md`\n56\t9. `RUN_MANIFEST.sha256`\n57\t\n58\t`AUTHORED_NOT_GO`\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261007014731-1322 — Integration receipt: Implement and independently review ADR0011 C18 reached-stage precedence and exact-once custody in the persistent ADR0011 worktree [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010153748-5419 — Integration receipt: Produce and independently review the immutable consolidated ADR0011 Stage 7 audit [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010082114-8857 — ADR0011 Stage 7A corrected source-context whole-diff review is green [possibly relevant]\n- 20260803224057-2792 — Orient selection: pilot one source-only PCNTC generated property [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# Independent review request\n2\t\n3\tReview exact package bytes at source HEAD `a1cd77950ffa45ebed52310878f772f3c7344756`.\n4\t\n5\tReturn exactly:\n6\t\n7\t`ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO`\n8\t\n9\tonly if all conditions hold for the final `RUN_MANIFEST.sha256`:\n10\t\n11\t1. v1 48-UNRESOLVED adjudication output/result remains immutable negative gate-ordering evidence and no absent source is normalized or semantically classified;\n12\t2. reconciliation enumerates 47 exact producer IDs plus the exact omitted reservation obligation, explains the generator cause, and proves duplicates/omissions `0` with all 48 accounted;\n13\t3. Stage A existing rows are restricted to Manager accounting ownership, account lifecycle, lease APIs/transfer capabilities, terminal cleanup, and nearby nonreusable leases;\n14\t4. Stage A future rows use only `PLANNED_RESERVATION`, `PLANNED_COPY`, `PLANNED_ALIAS`, `PLANNED_TRANSFER`, and `PLANNED_RELEASE`, with exact proposed bindings and lineage;\n15\t5. Stage A completeness is identity and architecture-obligation completeness, not source-semantic completeness;\n16\t6. Stage B requires canonical enumeration from an exact committed implementation source manifest, source-derived actual IDs, independent `NECESSARY|REUSE|FALSE_POSITIVE|UNRESOLVED` classification, and `UNRESOLVED=0` before any later implementation GO;\n17\t7. planned-to-actual lineage handles realized, disappeared, split, merged, and emergent rows without reusing planned IDs;\n18\t8. source and run checksums verify and generated outputs reproduce byte-for-byte;\n19\t9. interface GO, RED GO, implementation GO, production admission, activation, and commit authority all remain false.\n20\t\n21\tRecord reviewer identity/revision, source-manifest result, run-manifest digest, reconciliation/count result, Stage A schema/completeness result, Stage B and correction-lineage result, immutable-evidence result, and exact token or one blocker.\n22\t\n23\tThe token qualifies contract bytes only. It does not authorize implementation or tests.\n24\t\n25\tCurrent disposition: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20261007014731-1322 — Integration receipt: Implement and independently review ADR0011 C18 reached-stage precedence and exact-once custody in the persistent ADR0011 worktree [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010153748-5419 — Integration receipt: Produce and independently review the immutable consolidated ADR0011 Stage 7 audit [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001214518-6991 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte Stage-B T4 completed-STOP lease-retirement RED-to-GREEN implementation/result review [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t# Two-stage enumeration and adjudication contract\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n4\t\n5\t## Stage A: PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\n6\t\n7\tStage A separates source-backed present observations from future architecture obligations.\n8\t\n9\t### Existing-source contract\n10\t\n11\tAn `EXISTING_SOURCE` row is admissible only for an exact current source locator in these bounded families:\n12\t\n13\t- `Manager` as the current accounting-domain owner;\n14\t- current C15 account type, creation, and lifetime;\n15\t- current lease reservation, alias, transfer, and release capability;\n16\t- current terminal cleanup;\n17\t- nearby lease/borrow APIs that are explicitly observed as lifetime-bound and not reusable.\n18\t\n19\tAllowed statuses are `EXISTING_OBSERVED` and `EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE`. These are observations, not `NECESSARY`, `REUSE`, future design approval, or proof that the current API satisfies the directional contract.\n20\t\n21\t### Planned-obligation contract\n22\t\n23\tA planned row has no source line or source hash. It must use exactly one status from:\n24\t\n25\t- `PLANNED_RESERVATION`\n26\t- `PLANNED_COPY`\n27\t- `PLANNED_ALIAS`\n28\t- `PLANNED_TRANSFER`\n29\t- `PLANNED_RELEASE`\n30\t\n31\tIt binds an exact proposed file, symbol, component, attempt/account/lease identity, terminal paths where applicable, and predecessor lineage. `NECESSARY`, `REUSE`, `FALSE_POSITIVE`, and source-semantic `UNRESOLVED` are forbidden in Stage A planned rows because implementation source does not exist.\n32\t\n33\t### Stage A completeness\n34\t\n35\t`PREIMPLEMENTATION_COMPLETE` requires all 48 legacy identities accounted, duplicates `0`, omissions `0`, all six components covered by reservation/copy/alias obligations, whole-acquisition transfer present, and terminal convergence release present. It says nothing about actual implementation source semantics.\n36\t\n37\t## Stage B: POST-IMPLEMENTATION\n38\t\n39\tStage B begins only from an exact committed implementation revision and canonical source manifest. It does not accept line-0, absent-source, or planned rows as actual rows.\n40\t\n41\tThe canonical actual row ID is:\n42\t\n43\t```text\n44\tsha256(\"adr0011.c15.two-stage.actual.v1\\0\" ||\n45\t       source_path || \"\\0\" || symbol || \"\\0\" || operation_kind || \"\\0\" ||\n46\t       component || \"\\0\" || backing_identity_rule)\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tA deterministic source enumerator must emit every actual reservation, owned copy, alias/borrow, transfer, release, accounting owner/account lifecycle, and terminal cleanup relationship in scope. Two runs from the same committed manifest must be byte-identical. Actual duplicates and omissions must be zero.\n50\t\n51\tA separate independent pass classifies each actual row as exactly:\n52\t\n53\t- `NECESSARY`\n54\t- `REUSE`\n55\t- `FALSE_POSITIVE`\n56\t- `UNRESOLVED`\n57\t\n58\tEvery non-`UNRESOLVED` classification requires exact source evidence, contrary evidence or a falsifier, adjudicator identity, and revision. `IMPLEMENTATION_GO` requires `UNRESOLVED=0`; this contract does not return or authorize that gate.\n59\t\n60\t## Correction lineage\n61\t\n62\tPlanned and actual namespaces never alias. `planned_predecessor_ids` records architecture lineage without determining actual identity.\n63\t\n64\t- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65\t- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66\t- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67\t- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row and must be justified or block GO.\n68\t- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69\t\n70\tSplit and merge records list every predecessor and successor; no row is silently overwritten. A disappeared obligation is not a source absence claim until the complete committed manifest and canonical enumeration establish it.\n71\t\n72\t## Gate boundary\n73\t\n74\tThe exact token `ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO` qualifies only this ordering and schema. Interface/RED work remains blocked until that token. Implementation remains separately blocked and is never authorized by Stage A completeness or this package.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260805185048-9754 — Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824234609-5129 — Five current-source observations renew three ScopeRationalization rows at evidence tier only [possibly relevant]\n- 20260831182029-0487 — Pinned source supports read-only cross-app status aggregation but not a canonical identity contract [possibly relevant]\n- 20260827162246-6425 — Post-exact24 orientation selects independent exact-two blocked-row source recovery [possibly relevant]\n- 20260805185115-4797 — Internal phase-one planning describes 1,440 fixed hours and six deliverables, not yet reconciled to an executed SOW [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t{\n2\t  \"authority\": 0,\n3\t  \"implementation_go\": false,\n4\t  \"interface_go\": false,\n5\t  \"legacy_adjudicator_duplicates\": 0,\n6\t  \"legacy_adjudicator_identity_count\": 48,\n7\t  \"legacy_all_48_accounted\": true,\n8\t  \"legacy_matched\": 47,\n9\t  \"legacy_omissions_after_reconciliation\": 0,\n10\t  \"legacy_omissions_before_correction\": 1,\n11\t  \"legacy_producer_duplicates\": 0,\n12\t  \"legacy_producer_identity_count\": 47,\n13\t  \"red_go\": false,\n14\t  \"stage_a_existing_source_rows\": 13,\n15\t  \"stage_a_planned_obligation_rows\": 20,\n16\t  \"stage_a_preimplementation_complete\": true,\n17\t  \"stage_a_unresolved_identity_accounting\": 0,\n18\t  \"stage_b_actual_rows\": 0,\n19\t  \"stage_b_implementation_go\": false,\n20\t  \"stage_b_unresolved\": null,\n21\t  \"status\": \"AUTHORED_NOT_GO\",\n22\t  \"target\": \"ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO\"\n23\t}\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260817144058-8772 — DASL's normal web submission writes status 9 while legacy statuses 6–9 display as Submitted [possibly relevant]\n- 20260729195634-7197 — NAIS requires remaining legacy solutions and interfaces to be retired. [possibly relevant]\n- 20260729201642-0162 — Axiom: Legacy retirement is an endpoint after migration coexistence, not a synonym for migration start. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010153748-5419 — Integration receipt: Produce and independently review the immutable consolidated ADR0011 Stage 7 audit [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Deterministic documentation-only producer for the ADR0011 C15 two-stage contract.\"\"\"\n3\timport csv\n4\timport hashlib\n5\timport json\n6\tfrom pathlib import Path\n7\t\n8\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n9\tOUT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n10\tHEAD = \"a1cd77950ffa45ebed52310878f772f3c7344756\"\n11\tV1 = ROOT / \"docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-enumeration-v1\"\n12\tTARGET = \"ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT_GO\"\n13\tTERMINALS = \"normal|complete-empty|malformed|protocol|transport|unsupported|timeout|cancel|refusal|STOP|RESTART|Shutdown|stale-generation|race|duplicate-release\"\n14\t\n15\t\n16\tdef digest_bytes(data):\n17\t    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()\n18\t\n19\t\n20\tdef file_digest(path):\n21\t    return digest_bytes(path.read_bytes())\n22\t\n23\t\n24\tdef stable_id(namespace, *parts):\n25\t    return digest_bytes((namespace + \"\\0\" + \"\\0\".join(parts)).encode())\n26\t\n27\t\n28\tdef write_tsv(name, fields, rows):\n29\t    with (OUT / name).open(\"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n30\t        writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fields, delimiter=\"\\t\", lineterminator=\"\\n\")\n31\t        writer.writeheader()\n32\t        writer.writerows(rows)\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t# Preserve v1 as immutable negative evidence. The package is read, never rewritten.\n36\twith (V1 / \"UNRESOLVED.tsv\").open(newline=\"\") as f:\n37\t    producer_rows = list(csv.DictReader(f, delimiter=\"\\t\"))\n38\tif len(producer_rows) != 47 or len({r[\"row_id\"] for r in producer_rows}) != 47:\n39\t    raise SystemExit(\"expected exact immutable producer set: 47 unique rows\")\n40\t\n41\tmissing_symbol = \"reserveDirectionalComponentV2\"\n42\tmissing_component = \"ALL_SIX_COMPONENTS\"\n43\tmissing_id = stable_id(\n44\t    \"adr0011.c15.lease-source.v2.row\",\n45\t    \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\",\n46\t    missing_symbol,\n47\t    \"RESERVE\",\n48\t    missing_component,\n49\t    \"planned exact pre-effect component/bytes/attempt/account reservation\",\n50\t)\n51\t\n52\treconciliation = []\n53\tfor index, row in enumerate(sorted(producer_rows, key=lambda r: r[\"row_id\"]), 1):\n54\t    reconciliation.append({\n55\t        \"identity_ordinal\": str(index),\n56\t        \"adjudicator_identity\": row[\"row_id\"],\n57\t        \"producer_row_id\": row[\"row_id\"],\n58\t        \"source_path\": row[\"source_path\"],\n59\t        \"symbol\": row[\"symbol\"],\n60\t        \"operation_kind\": row[\"operation_kind\"],\n61\t        \"component\": row[\"component\"],\n62\t        \"reconciliation\": \"MATCHED_PRODUCER_ROW\",\n63\t        \"cause\": \"exact identity present in producer47\",\n64\t    })\n65\treconciliation.append({\n66\t    \"identity_ordinal\": \"48\",\n67\t    \"adjudicator_identity\": missing_id,\n68\t    \"producer_row_id\": \"\",\n69\t    \"source_path\": \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\",\n70\t    \"symbol\": missing_symbol,\n71\t    \"operation_kind\": \"RESERVE\",\n72\t    \"component\": missing_component,\n73\t    \"reconciliation\": \"OMITTED_BY_PRODUCER47\",\n74\t    \"cause\": \"generator iterated ALLOCATE and ALIAS plus one TRANSFER and RELEASE, but never emitted the architecture-required pre-effect RESERVE identity\",\n75\t})\n76\treconciliation.sort(key=lambda r: int(r[\"identity_ordinal\"]))\n77\twrite_tsv(\"LEGACY_48_IDENTITY_RECONCILIATION.tsv\", list(reconciliation[0]), reconciliation)\n78\t\n79\texisting_specs = [\n80\t    (\"sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go\", 1564, \"Manager\", \"ACCOUNTING_OWNER\", \"MANAGER_ACCOUNTING_DOMAIN\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current Manager owns the accounting-domain lock and lifecycle integration point\"),\n81\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 125, \"privateB4ByteAccountV2\", \"ACCOUNT_LIFETIME\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current versioned transaction account type\"),\n82\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 147, \"newPrivateB4ByteAccountV2\", \"ACCOUNT_CREATE\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account constructor\"),\n83\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 174, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).reserve\", \"LEASE_RESERVE\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current byte-lease reservation API\"),\n84\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 379, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).aliasPrivateB4C15\", \"LEASE_ALIAS\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account-local alias capability\"),\n85\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 495, \"(*privateB4ByteLeaseV2).Release\", \"LEASE_RELEASE\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current lease release API\"),\n86\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 557, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).transferDiagnosticBacking\", \"LEASE_TRANSFER\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current single diagnostic transfer capability\"),\n87\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 561, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).transferDiagnosticBackingPair\", \"LEASE_TRANSFER\", \"C15_LEASE_SET\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current paired diagnostic transfer capability\"),\n88\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 660, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).requestTerminalRelease\", \"TERMINAL_CLEANUP\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account terminal-release request\"),\n89\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 670, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).maybeReleaseBackingLocked\", \"TERMINAL_CLEANUP\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current terminal backing cleanup\"),\n90\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go\", 112, \"OwnedMethodPairLease.WithPair\", \"NONREUSABLE_BORROW\", \"NEARBY_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE\", \"nearby callback borrow is lifetime-bound and is not a reusable directional acquisition\"),\n91\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go\", 311, \"callHierarchyObservationLease.withObservation\", \"NONREUSABLE_BORROW\", \"NEARBY_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE\", \"nearby observation borrow is lifetime-bound and is not reusable\"),\n92\t    (\"sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go\", 639, \"callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease.Callback\", \"NONREUSABLE_BORROW\", \"NEARBY_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_NOT_REUSABLE\", \"nearby generic callback lease is synchronous and not reusable\"),\n93\t]\n94\texisting = []\n95\tfor path, line, symbol, kind, component, classification, observation in existing_specs:\n96\t    p = ROOT / path\n97\t    existing.append({\n98\t        \"stage_a_row_id\": stable_id(\"adr0011.c15.two-stage.stage-a.existing.v1\", path, symbol, kind, component),\n99\t        \"row_kind\": \"EXISTING_SOURCE\",\n100\t        \"status\": classification,\n101\t        \"source_path\": path,\n102\t        \"source_start_line\": str(line),\n103\t        \"source_end_line\": str(line),\n104\t        \"source_sha256\": file_digest(p),\n105\t        \"symbol\": symbol,\n106\t        \"operation_kind\": kind,\n107\t        \"component\": component,\n108\t        \"attempt_identity\": \"CURRENT_SOURCE_ONLY\",\n109\t        \"account_identity\": \"CURRENT_SOURCE_ONLY\",\n110\t        \"lease_identity\": \"CURRENT_SOURCE_ONLY\",\n111\t        \"terminal_paths\": TERMINALS if kind == \"TERMINAL_CLEANUP\" else \"\",\n112\t        \"predecessor_lineage\": \"NULL@0\",\n113\t        \"obligation\": observation,\n114\t        \"authority_ceiling\": \"SOURCE_OBSERVATION_ONLY; no future necessity or reuse conclusion\",\n115\t    })\n116\twrite_tsv(\"STAGE_A_EXISTING_SOURCE.tsv\", list(existing[0]), existing)\n117\t\n118\tplanned_specs = []\n119\tcomponents = [\"PREPARE_FRAME\", \"PREPARE_RESULT\", \"SELECTED_HANDOFF\", \"DIRECTIONAL_FRAME\", \"DIRECTIONAL_RESULT\", \"RETAINED_EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE\"]\n120\tfor component in components:\n121\t    key = component.lower()\n122\t    planned_specs.append((f\"reserveDirectional{component.title().replace('_','')}V3\", \"PLANNED_RESERVATION\", component, f\"attempt_id+account_id+{component}+exact_bytes\", \"none\", \"reserve before owned effect\"))\n123\t    planned_specs.append((f\"copyDirectional{component.title().replace('_','')}V3\", \"PLANNED_COPY\", component, f\"attempt_id+account_id+{component}+backing_id\", \"reservation row for same component\", \"owned bytes and all leases remain inseparable\"))\n124\t    planned_specs.append((f\"aliasDirectional{component.title().replace('_','')}V3\", \"PLANNED_ALIAS\", component, f\"attempt_id+account_id+{component}+owner_lease_id+offset+length\", \"copy or transferred owner for same component\", \"zero-charge bounded alias; no escape or independent publication\"))\n125\tplanned_specs.append((\"transferDirectionalAcquisitionV3\", \"PLANNED_TRANSFER\", \"ALL_SIX_COMPONENTS\", \"source_attempt+destination_attempt+source_account+destination_account+complete_lease_set\", \"reservation/copy/alias rows for transferred acquisition\", \"atomically move complete bytes plus leases; preserve source on failure\"))\n126\tplanned_specs.append((\"releaseDirectionalTerminalV3\", \"PLANNED_RELEASE\", \"ALL_SIX_COMPONENTS\", \"attempt_id+account_id+all_active_lease_ids+release_id\", \"all rows for the attempt\", \"one terminal winner clears aliases/bytes and releases every lease exactly once\"))\n127\tplanned = []\n128\tfor symbol, status, component, identity, predecessor, obligation in planned_specs:\n129\t    planned.append({\n130\t        \"stage_a_row_id\": stable_id(\"adr0011.c15.two-stage.stage-a.planned.v1\", \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\", symbol, status, component, identity),\n131\t        \"row_kind\": \"PLANNED_OBLIGATION\",\n132\t        \"status\": status,\n133\t        \"proposed_source_path\": \"sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go\",\n134\t        \"proposed_symbol\": symbol,\n135\t        \"component\": component,\n136\t        \"attempt_account_lease_identity\": identity,\n137\t        \"terminal_paths\": TERMINALS if status == \"PLANNED_RELEASE\" else \"\",\n138\t        \"predecessor_lineage\": predecessor,\n139\t        \"obligation\": obligation,\n140\t        \"source_semantics\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE_PREIMPLEMENTATION\",\n141\t        \"authority_ceiling\": \"PLANNED_ARCHITECTURE_OBLIGATION_ONLY; no NECESSARY/REUSE classification\",\n142\t    })\n143\twrite_tsv(\"STAGE_A_PLANNED_OBLIGATIONS.tsv\", list(planned[0]), planned)\n144\t\n145\tstage_b_fields = [\"actual_row_id\", \"source_path\", \"source_start_line\", \"source_end_line\", \"source_sha256\", \"symbol\", \"operation_kind\", \"component\", \"attempt_identity\", \"account_identity\", \"lease_identity\", \"classification\", \"planned_predecessor_ids\", \"lineage_event\", \"contrary_evidence\", \"adjudicator_id\", \"adjudication_revision\"]\n146\twrite_tsv(\"STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv\", stage_b_fields, [])\n147\t\n148\tcounts = {\n149\t    \"target\": TARGET,\n150\t    \"status\": \"AUTHORED_NOT_GO\",\n151\t    \"legacy_adjudicator_identity_count\": 48,\n152\t    \"legacy_producer_identity_count\": 47,\n153\t    \"legacy_matched\": 47,\n154\t    \"legacy_producer_duplicates\": 0,\n155\t    \"legacy_adjudicator_duplicates\": 0,\n156\t    \"legacy_omissions_before_correction\": 1,\n157\t    \"legacy_omissions_after_reconciliation\": 0,\n158\t    \"legacy_all_48_accounted\": True,\n159\t    \"stage_a_existing_source_rows\": len(existing),\n160\t    \"stage_a_planned_obligation_rows\": len(planned),\n161\t    \"stage_a_unresolved_identity_accounting\": 0,\n162\t    \"stage_a_preimplementation_complete\": True,\n163\t    \"stage_b_actual_rows\": 0,\n164\t    \"stage_b_unresolved\": None,\n165\t    \"stage_b_implementation_go\": False,\n166\t    \"interface_go\": False,\n167\t    \"red_go\": False,\n168\t    \"implementation_go\": False,\n169\t    \"authority\": 0,\n170\t}\n171\t(OUT / \"COUNTS.json\").write_text(json.dumps(counts, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n172\t\n173\tsource_paths = sorted({r[\"source_path\"] for r in existing})\n174\twith (OUT / \"SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256\").open(\"w\") as f:\n175\t    f.write(f\"# HEAD {HEAD}\\n\")\n176\t    for path in source_paths:\n177\t        p = ROOT / path\n178\t        f.write(f\"{file_digest(p)}  {p.stat().st_size}  {path}\\n\")\n179\t    for name in [\"UNRESOLVED.tsv\", \"COUNTS.json\", \"RUN_MANIFEST.sha256\", \"generate.py\"]:\n180\t        p = V1 / name\n181\t        f.write(f\"{file_digest(p)}  {p.stat().st_size}  docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-enumeration-v1/{name}\\n\")\n182\t\n183\tfiles = sorted(p for p in OUT.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name != \"RUN_MANIFEST.sha256\")\n184\twith (OUT / \"RUN_MANIFEST.sha256\").open(\"w\") as f:\n185\t    for p in files:\n186\t        f.write(f\"{file_digest(p)}  {p.name}\\n\")\n187\tprint(json.dumps(counts, sort_keys=True))\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005192502-3026 — Integration receipt: Independently review complete ADR0011 C15 private transaction accounting production migration to V2 account/lease family [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006014845-6698 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial retained-notification lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, refusal atomicity, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261004230052-1374 — Integration receipt: Independently adjudicate bounded ADR0011 C15 custodial private-B4 ingress params-copy accounting [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824234609-5129 — Five current-source observations renew three ScopeRationalization rows at evidence tier only [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.","truncated":true,"truncatedBy":"bytes","totalLines":977,"totalBytes":72275,"outputLines":673,"outputBytes":51185,"lastLinePartial":false,"firstLineExceedsLimit":false,"maxLines":2000,"maxBytes":51200},"fullOutputPath":"/var/folders/bc/qbdy42vs4jn56zwrb2y09l9m0000gn/T/pi-bash-a8e2e91509154ec6.log"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1791904804306},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:20:04.307Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
