{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"1f290c50-b945-4fe","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f466121d659a4e569a2e15f0b8687a86|fc_03201568652b0503016ace4c64b434819b89291a2580162f1d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nid: 20260803181149-6565\ntitle: Pinned DASL source regenerates the synthetic association service seam without a backup.\ntype: observation\nstatus: reviewed\ntags: []\ncreated: 2026-08-03T18:11:49.628291Z\nmodified: 2026-08-03T18:12:02.487598Z\n---\nfreshness: stale (70 days ago — revalidate before using as evidence of current conditions; this does not imply the historical note should expire)\n\n\n\n\n\nA persistent generator reads two EDMX models, two ReportDataAudit migrations, and seven SQL definitions from DASL commit `77541d935e800f76c84ac7983a5ebe7a98f9f7bf`. It creates 170 model tables, 11 synthetic seed statements, 21 legacy synonyms, RD1000, NA1000, two empty schema-minimal dependency tables, and the tracked association procedure/function closure without reading a backup or an existing application database.\n\nAn independent checker generated two initially absent SQL Edge databases, required zero unresolved synonyms and bounded projection cardinalities, observed equal semantic fingerprints, ran the adapted controller test with 0 build errors and 0 test failures, and removed both targets. The local `dasl-prototype/db` schema and seed were excluded because they are untracked at the pinned commit and have no Git history.\n\nThis is backup-independent ServiceBoundaryValidation in one adapted synthetic SQL Edge environment. App/Report namespace projection, synthetic seed/projections, a migration-derived audit table without foreign keys, and empty dependency tables constrain its reach; calculated dependency propagation, transport, deployment, production, historical fidelity, and cross-environment equivalence remain unproved.\n\n## Links\n\n- [[20260803164309-7975|Source index: adapted synthetic association-school service seam]] [supports] {draft} — Two independent source-generated databases and a passing controller test corroborate the bounded service-seam execution without relying on restoration.\n- [[20260803164358-4022|The synthetic NAIS SQL Edge backup restores the executable association spike.]] [refines] {draft} — Source-only regeneration distinguishes reproducible generation from the separately valid opaque-backup restoration path.\n\n## Backlinks (2)\n\n- [[20260803164309-7975|Source index: adapted synthetic association-school service seam]] [source-of] {reviewed} — The spike investigation is the provenance for backup-independent source generation and repeatability.\n- [[20260812225627-4325|Adaptation-authorized orientation selects one-value DASL release-middle carrier]] [grounded-by] {draft} — The prior source-generated adapted SQL Edge environment demonstrates the adaptation-ledger and two-fresh-database reproducibility pattern used by this plan.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791904872454},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:21:12.454Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
