ovenance is unproven.** Preserved v1 `UNRESOLVED.tsv` and `INDEPENDENT_ROW_ADJUDICATION_ASSIGNMENT.tsv` each contain **47**, not 48, unique `UNRESOLVED` rows. Correct by either:\n   - supplying and pinning the claimed immutable 48-identity adjudicator artifact, or\n   - describing reconciliation honestly as 47 preserved identities plus one newly introduced architecture obligation—not an independently supplied 48 denominator.\n\n2. **Three Stage A source locators are wrong.**\n   - `OwnedMethodPairLease.WithPair`: recorded line 112; declaration is line **95**.\n   - `callHierarchyObservationLease.withObservation`: recorded line 311; declaration is line **300**.\n   - `callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease.Callback`: recorded line 639; declaration is line **628**.\n\n3. **Planned predecessor lineage is not exact.** Values such as `reservation row for same component`, `all rows for the attempt`, and `none` are descriptions, not stable predecessor row IDs. Replace them with exact planned IDs or an explicit genesis sentinel.\n\n4. **Stage B cannot represent its full promised contract.**\n   - Its actual-row schema omits `backing_identity_rule`, although that field is part of the canonical actual-row ID.\n   - An actual-row-only table cannot record `DISAPPEARED` planned obligations because those have no actual row.\n   - Add an explicit lineage table/schema supporting `REALIZED`, `DISAPPEARED`, `SPLIT`, `MERGED`, and `EMERGENT` with complete predecessor/successor sets.\n\n5. Recompute both manifests and counts after correction.\n\nVerified green: HEAD, existing manifest integrity, 47 producer identities without duplicates/omissions, generator-cause analysis, allowed Stage A status vocabulary, 6× reservation/copy/alias coverage, authority boundaries, and clean-copy byte-for-byte determinism.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03201568652b0503016ace4c854300819ba9e203591c341c79\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"