\n--\n61:\n62:Planned and actual namespaces never alias. `STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv` contains `backing_identity_rule`, which participates in the actual row ID formula. `STAGE_B_PLANNED_ACTUAL_LINEAGE.tsv` separately records complete planned/actual predecessor and successor sets without determining actual identity.\n63:\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260826235337-9258|Corrective orientation selects actual inspection of five frozen provenance routes]] [possibly relevant]\n62:Planned and actual namespaces never alias. `STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv` contains `backing_identity_rule`, which participates in the actual row ID formula. `STAGE_B_PLANNED_ACTUAL_LINEAGE.tsv` separately records complete planned/actual predecessor and successor sets without determining actual identity.\n63:\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260826235337-9258|Corrective orientation selects actual inspection of five frozen provenance routes]] [possibly relevant]\n63:\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69:\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260812211001-9778|Post-Issue-35 orientation selects one decision-receiving row before new technical evidence]] [possibly relevant]\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69:\n70:Each lineage record has a stable `lineage_record_id`, event, complete `planned_predecessor_ids`, `actual_predecessor_ids`, `planned_successor_ids`, and `actual_successor_ids`, plus justification and adjudicator revision. Split and merge records list every predecessor and successor; no row is silently overwritten. A disappeared obligation is not a source absence claim until the complete committed manifest and canonical enumeration establish it.\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260805185115-4797|Internal phase-one planning describes 1,440 fixed hours and six deliverables, not yet reconciled to an executed SOW]] [possibly relevant]\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69:\n70:Each lineage record has a stable `lineage_record_id`, event, complete `planned_predecessor_ids`, `actual_predecessor_ids`, `planned_successor_ids`, and `actual_successor_ids`, plus justification and adjudicator revision. Split and merge records list every predecessor and successor; no row is silently overwritten. A disappeared obligation is not a source absence claim until the complete committed manifest and canonical enumeration establish it.\n71:\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20261005200030-7052|Integration receipt: Investigate and design ADR 0007 review-custody successor Phase 0 against the actual Pi message_end and agent_settled boundary]] [possibly relevant]\n\n==> docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-two-stage-contract-v2/generate.py <==\n78:    \"cause\": \"v1 generator iterated ALLOCATE and ALIAS plus one TRANSFER and RELEASE, but never emitted the architecture-required pre-effect RESERVE obligation\",\n79:})\n80:reconciliation.sort(key=lambda r: int(r[\"identity_ordinal\"]))\n81:write_tsv(\"IDENTITY_ACCOUNTING_47_PLUS_1.tsv\", list(reconciliation[0]), reconciliation)\n82:\n83:existing_specs = [\n84:    (\"sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go\", 1564, \"Manager\", \"ACCOUNTING_OWNER\", \"MANAGER_ACCOUNTING_DOMAIN\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current Manager owns the accounting-domain lock and lifecycle integration point\"),\n  → [[2