fdf3ee29da89e9c4e6423ac261916068ca5b|51590290aea507a4972547c0923647c52d1c657fdecdfbb3aa6244ba5a417347|645cf06e35e54bc3fe5a827bc0f6a4156c2b23e5739d70d2b012c5c1884ae894|7069d8601cb76101ee1a2c7886f223d0a6119e74b76891d3dd49f35117cb0736|75e32e98aaf21d7ec04d26d13fd202699b4bf6ad466688edb8f70231835a14e7|7f46d76e8acde79c1eec46102632bd6db557ac394d329b31b68c9697abbd4ea2|a3ec11a555246160475c5519e29735fc4f86ce88eeef053bd0f97c88e4221102|b1bf63296afd47f73f2be7e8a9c70db37f0ce77677b5ddf38a8b3a15fcba77d3|b3846db09b2b683ea536a8d6ddcdf3c5ff7408b0c4f6e0097656a4f7a2e16800|c2d3d4696cd315f18b986c14afd02a5ed642d7a99c2888ae172177a48f5ff1bc|c730d1a3978f99c2de26d634266e05a0909a0d5662eee7e86889f7b7603cb5aa|d3ed276e5de20a331b277b63638f7bc5ef05a45c9366a06ece882bb90502ac20|ddbbfd7184803b94919684bb5762ef16309986b1d5b091d650c1e05a9b578779\tone terminal winner clears aliases/bytes and releases every lease exactly once\tNOT_APPLICABLE_PREIMPLEMENTATION\tPLANNED_ARCHITECTURE_OBLIGATION_ONLY; no NECESSARY/REUSE classification\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20261012145659-8845|Integration receipt: three isolated plans converge on evidence-first DataVista Labs exposure planning]] [possibly relevant]\n\n==> docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-two-stage-contract-v2/TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT.md <==\n32:\n33:### Stage A completeness\n34:\n35:`PREIMPLEMENTATION_COMPLETE` requires all 47 preserved v1 identities plus one newly introduced planned reservation architecture obligation accounted, duplicates `0`, omissions `0`, planned predecessor closure with cycles/missing predecessors/branches `0`, all six components covered by reservation/copy/alias obligations, whole-acquisition transfer present, and terminal convergence release present. The model-reported 48 is unpinned because no exact full adjudicator output is available to copy and hash-prove. Completeness says nothing about actual implementation source semantics.\n36:\n37:## Stage B: POST-IMPLEMENTATION\n38:\n  → [[20260902031736-3885|Accepted-root completion selects all remaining 163 DASL C# symbols]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260814161613-4019|DASL Release to Reporting is documented as a per-collection-part transfer governed by annually revised runbooks.]] [possibly relevant]\n--\n61:\n62:Planned and actual namespaces never alias. `STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv` contains `backing_identity_rule`, which participates in the actual row ID formula. `STAGE_B_PLANNED_ACTUAL_LINEAGE.tsv` separately records complete planned/actual predecessor and successor sets without determining actual identity.\n63:\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260826235337-9258|Corrective orientation selects actual inspection of five frozen provenance routes]] [possibly relevant]\n62:Planned and actual namespaces never alias. `STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv` contains `backing_identity_rule`, which participates in the actual row ID formula. `STAGE_B_PLANNED_ACTUAL_LINEAGE.tsv` separately records complete planned/actual predecessor and successor sets without determining actual identity.\n63:\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260826235337-9258|Corrective orientation selects actual inspection of five frozen provenance routes]] [possibly relevant]\n63:\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69:\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260812211001-9778|Post-Issue-35 orientation selects one decision-receiving row before new technical evidence]] [possibly relevant]\n64:- `REALIZED`: one planned obligation maps to one actual row.\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69:\n70:Each lineage record has a stable `lineage_record_id`, event, complete `planned_predecessor_ids`, `actual_predecessor_ids`, `planned_successor_ids`, and `actual_successor_ids`, plus justification and adjudicator revision. Split and merge records list every predecessor and successor; no row is silently overwritten. A disappeared obligation is not a source absence claim until the complete committed manifest and canonical enumeration establish it.\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260805185115-4797|Internal phase-one planning describes 1,440 fixed hours and six deliverables, not yet reconciled to an executed SOW]] [possibly relevant]\n65:- `SPLIT`: one planned obligation maps to multiple independently source-derived actual rows.\n66:- `MERGED`: multiple planned obligations map to one independently source-derived actual row.\n67:- `DISAPPEARED`: a planned obligation has no actual row; `actual_successor_ids` is explicitly empty and the disappearance must be justified or block GO.\n68:- `EMERGENT`: an actual row has no planned predecessor and must be independently adjudicated.\n69:\n70:Each lineage record has a stable `lineage_record_id`, event, complete `planned_predecessor_ids`, `actual_predecessor_ids`, `planned_successor_ids`, and `actual_successor_ids`, plus justification and adjudicator revision. Split and merge records list every predecessor and successor; no row is silently overwritten. A disappeared obligation is not a source absence claim until the complete committed manifest and canonical enumeration establish it.\n71:\n  → [[20260805185048-9754|Source index: August 5 internal NAIS phase-one planning sync]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20261005200030-7052|Integration receipt: Investigate and design ADR 0007 review-custody successor Phase 0 against the actual Pi message_end and agent_settled boundary]] [possibly relevant]\n\n==> docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-two-stage-contract-v2/generate.py <==\n78:    \"cause\": \"v1 generator iterated ALLOCATE and ALIAS plus one TRANSFER and RELEASE, but never emitted the architecture-required pre-effect RESERVE obligation\",\n79:})\n80:reconciliation.sort(key=lambda r: int(r[\"identity_ordinal\"]))\n81:write_tsv(\"IDENTITY_ACCOUNTING_47_PLUS_1.tsv\", list(reconciliation[0]), reconciliation)\n82:\n83:existing_specs = [\n84:    (\"sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go\", 1564, \"Manager\", \"ACCOUNTING_OWNER\", \"MANAGER_ACCOUNTING_DOMAIN\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current Manager owns the accounting-domain lock and lifecycle integration point\"),\n  → [[20260821215545-6188|Phase 1 orientation selects six-segment operating-dependency currency to complete reconciliation accounting]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260828052138-2390|Fresh orientation selects exact 235-candidate to 36-identity reconciliation]] [possibly relevant]\n83:existing_specs = [\n84:    (\"sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go\", 1564, \"Manager\", \"ACCOUNTING_OWNER\", \"MANAGER_ACCOUNTING_DOMAIN\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current Manager owns the accounting-domain lock and lifecycle integration point\"),\n85:    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 125, \"privateB4ByteAccountV2\", \"ACCOUNT_LIFETIME\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current versioned transaction account type\"),\n86:    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 147, \"newPrivateB4ByteAccountV2\", \"ACCOUNT_CREATE\", \"C15_ACCOUNT\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account constructor\"),\n87:    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 174, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).reserve\", \"LEASE_RESERVE\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current byte-lease reservation API\"),\n88:    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 379, \"(*privateB4ByteAccountV2).aliasPrivateB4C15\", \"LEASE_ALIAS\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current account-local alias capability\"),\n89:    (\"sessionruntime/b4_explicit_bytes_c15_private.go\", 495, \"(*privateB4ByteLeaseV2).Release\", \"LEASE_RELEASE\", \"C15_LEASE\", \"EXISTING_OBSERVED\", \"current lease release API\"),\n  → [[20261005192502-3026|Integration receipt: Independently review complete ADR0011 C15 priv